window.RVE=window.RVE||{};window.RVE["com.babbel.mobile.android.en"]=[[5,"Switched over to Babbel since other language learning apps were starting to make their lessons with AI and it showed. So far, I really like the lesson structure! It feels more in-depth and the pop-up tips have been very helpful. Lifetime membership was kind of costly, but since it cost me about as much as a couple years of the competition and I can see getting more use out of it than that, was a good deal for a good learning program!","2025-07",1216,"+effect,+fun"],[4,"It's okay. I like that it explains more than Duolingo, but the lessons can get pretty repetitive, not to mention stuff that just isn't relevant. There were multiple lessons on talking about environmental pollution yet no lesson on animal names or buying groceries. Also, not happy that I have to use Spain Spanish instead of Latin American because the latter only had two levels to go through. I'm glad I didn't buy the lifetime subscription. Just a year then I'll probably drop it.","2025-05",1116,""],[5,"Babbel, unlike other language learning options, ACTUALLY teaches you the language rather than having you memorize words. It teaches you the diffrent concepts, and why diffrent letters make that particular sound. It teaches grammatical concepts early on and makes sure you understand everything. It does cost money, but the first lesson is free so you can test it out. I dont normally spend money on these types of things but it is 100% WORTH IT!!","2025-07",822,"+effect,+exam,+free"],[4,"This app is great for reading and writing. It teaches by associating the foreign language to the native one, which is useful if you only intend to read and write. However, the best way I have learned vocabulry is through associating objects, via pictures or cartoons, with the word. This is much more conducive to quicker processing and speaking in the foreign language. Lastly, the app has a serious bug in which some lessons will not show as completed until the user takes them 2, 3, 4 times.","2020-03",471,"+effect,+short"],[5,"Duolingo was fun and addictive, but it was too simple, not the best use of my limited time. Rocket Languages felt more grown up but literally put me to sleep. Babbel is more interesting, challenging, and useful than those two combined. It has more variety, content, and depth. The review system is thorough. Also, after it introduces new concepts through natural exposure, it follows up with micro-grammar lessons so that you don't go nuts wondering \"why?\" It doesn't leave you confused or hanging.","2023-06",464,"+short,+review,+fun"],[4,"It is far superior to other apps where there are no lessons as to how to conjugate words, recognize gender, etc. I have been having problems with the Russian lessons. This makes me bring it down from 5 to 4 stars. Many times when speaking, the app does not recognize the correct pronunciation. I even had a native Russian speaker speak into the microphone, and it was still saying it was incorrect. The issue is with certain words, specifically the numbers. It really ruins the experience.","2023-07",381,"+listen"],[5,"It's great if you like learning in more of a linear, formal way, it's very similar to how I was taught in school (to learn the basics and build on that.) It's a little boring in its template tho. I use Duolingo too and it sucks me in because it's like a game, but it seems to focus on immersion learning with few to no explainations. If you want a school-like learning experience, Babble is the better option.","2024-03",308,"+fun,+exam"],[1,"Very disappointed with this app, given all the advertising. After installing the app, you're given access to almost no features without a subscription (and payment). After trying the introduction lesson (all I have access to), I really have no idea if the app is worthwhile and I'm not willing to pay for it. Give me full access for a week or a month. If the system is any good, I'll want to make a commitment so that I can continue learning. The sales strategy is from the last century.","2020-12",296,"pay,ad"],[2,"Overall, the app is great. I like the lessons and structure. However, the speaking portions have recently become horribly unusable. As an example, I was asked to pronounce \"nueve\" (9 - very simple). It registered \"el baby\", \"weather\", \"DVD\", and \"the Bible\". None of which are even close to what I was saying! For \"uno\", it kept saying \"not understood\". It used to be better but has been going downhill over the past month. For a paid subscription, I expect the features to work!","2022-07",296,"pay"],[4,"So far, this has been a great app. I have learned a lot since downloading in just a few short weeks, much more than Duolingo. The thing I like the most is it is more situational so I can apply my learnings much quicker than others I've tried. the only thing I REALLY would like to see is an improved review experience. The four options are not nearly as effective as going back and retaking lessons. The reason is because it doesn't challenge you or give you much change, unlike the courses.","2023-04",278,"+effect,+short,+review,+wish"],[5,"In my professional opinion, this is by far the best language-learning app available. I am both a language instructor and a language learner, and I have tried MANY apps for years . Babbel teaches comprehensive grammar, vocabulary, pronunciation, and conversation with high quality native speaker recordings. It also doesn't \"dumb down\" anything. It is more than worth the price.","2025-03",274,"+listen"],[4,"One Lesson - Pricey!!! The program has repetitive exercises that are matching language words or selecting the correct word from given choices. With repetition, this will make some aspects of the lessons be learned. Not having access to more than this as a trial, such as typing my own sentences or speaking into the mic to check my pronunciation, I am not willing to make the $90 purchase. If there was a 30 day trial, I would be all in, and then decide if it is worth more lessons.","2023-03",263,"+effect,+review,+listen"],[5,"The selection of languages is predominantly european languages, I wish there were languages like Arabic or Hindi but that is preference and not quality. I would recommend this app to anybody who is struggling to find time to study a foreign language. The lessons are divided into easily digested pieces that can be consumed on a commute to work or before bed. I am speaking from expirience with the Russian course. I have been studying languages for a decade and this app is the best I've used.","2019-06",259,"+wish"],[4,"Been using this for about a month now, it's nice but if you're like me and didn't pay attention in English class and can't remember the difference between adverbs, verbs, conjunctions, pronouns ect., then like me you're going to be looking up the difference while trying to learn. Unit 9 lesson 3 for example, masculine or feminine pronunciation? No hints or explanations, just pick one cause you have a 50/50 chance of getting it if you're not 100%familiar, that stuffs irritating but overall good.","2023-12",257,"+effect,+listen,+exam"],[5,"The winner of my language app battle. Paid for six months. This app just has everything I want. Practical material but without ditching attention to grammar. Great community features for learning with others. Several different exercises for speaking, writing, reading, etc. while still being structured in a predictable way. Most of all, it doesn't feel like it's trying to be a game! What is it with that?! Edit: even fixed the unresponsive buttons when spelling scrambled words, thanks!","2024-08",252,"+fun"],[2,"The poor app interface really gets in the way of the language lessons. The lessons are useful, but without easy way to skip ahead, you are forced to tediously repeat things you already know to get to the end of a section. And the lack of a search function is a HUGE fail. I had to go through 20 courses just to find the section on counting. It was buried in a course called \"extra practice \", NOT where numbers need to be! Counting to 20 is super essential, ought to be an early lesson.","2024-01",247,"repeat,ui"],[2,"It's okay... just okay. I paid for a year of premium. I will not be renewing it once the year ends. I don't have enough characters to explain the issues in detail, but suffice to say it's not as good as most of the free language apps (such as Duolingo) and far inferior to any paid apps that I've tried. For a similar price, I highly recommend Wlingua or Memrise (or both lol). I've tried just about every language app on the play store and those two are by far the best I've found.","2022-09",214,"pay"],[1,"Terrible app. Voice recognition hardly works, which I tested with my native speaking friends so I know it's not just me. It doesn't matter how many times you set up reminder notifications, they'll just stop sending them after a couple days so they can take your money without actually providing a service. Also, lessons are generated by AI, by the app's own admission. It's incredibly unreliable AI.","2023-11",213,"pay,voice,lock"],[4,"Facsinating app. I love how it will progress at different paces based on your learning, but it would be nice if there were any options to change the subscription. From what I can see the only way is to cancel, wait for the app to stop working, then resubscribe if it gives a popup. I tried to switch from the one month to the 12 month, and I can find no easy options. Still waiting to see if the cancelling then looking for a popup works. A free trial would be a really nice way to help users as well","2023-10",211,"+short,+free,+wish"],[5,"This is a really, really good app. What's more, pricing is very reasonable. Language learning is a very personal thing. This app eases you into conversation right away, which is the right thing to do. I think it is better than Duolingo and better than Rosetta Stone in both approach, app design, and pricing. They have some individual nice feature that this one lacks, but Babbel is better in where it really counts. Try them all, that's the only way to figure out which one will motivate you best.","2021-01",210,"+fun"],[2,"I had to pay for two subscriptions because one subscription doesn't cover multiple languages. There's no knowledge test that I can find so I have to start from scratch which is annoying. Navigating through the app is anti-intuitive. Switching languages is difficult. There's no option for dialects when you learn French (like Quebec). There's also no \"I can't speak right now\" or \"I can't listen right now\" buttons which makes it more inconvenient.","2023-02",209,"pay,ui"],[1,"It's an expensive dualingo app. It advertises a lot of features that aren't there. Pinsluer is way better. The refund policy is also no existent. Don't waste your money. I'm super disappointed in the Spanish lessons and the \"podcats\" is one episode of some lady who thought it would be fun to learn French. Add: I wish I could go lower after that response. I have emailed and you never get back to it.","2023-12",206,"pay,ad,wish"],[4,"Great app for casual language learning. They tuck in nice tips and grammar in contextual lessons and the interface is a breeze. Only feedback would be a setting for the speed of speech. For me, it's a bit slow. Perhaps optionally also factor in some exercises with free or less guided writing at the end of each lesson to force learners to express themselves more integrally with the previously learned material. Also, subscription packets should start at one month, instead of three.","2024-02",191,"+effect,+free"],[5,"So far, so good. it's definitely easy to pick up on, and to be able to read while you listen is definitely something that helps it sink in, at least for me. Babbel knows what parts need to be gone over, repeated to catch on, not just here's these words and what they mean, with no context. I know I have more to learn and more to catch onto, but babbel is absolutely without a doubt helping to improve at a much faster rate than just trying on my own. I absolutely recommend and would use again!!","2024-10",183,"+effect,+short,+wish"],[2,"Not very different then duolingo, which is free. Only the very first level of Babbel is free, then you have to subscribe to access other lessons. That lesson was good, but not any better then the ones in its free competitors. Maybe there are more features you can utilize once you've learned more, but I wouldn't know because they asked for money before I was really sold. Would love a free trial, so I can really see if the ap's value.... but for now I'm going back to duolingo","2021-03",180,"pay"],[4,"I'm learning a lot from the app on my phone. The voice recognition needs major improvements though. It just doesn't recognize what I'm saying. I have to skip the pronunciation more than not and it's discouraging that such an important part of the app underperforms. Note to the devs: I'm on Android with a Bluetooth headset on. It's possible the headset is picking up my voice poorly.","2023-01",173,"+effect,+listen,+wish"],[5,"This makes learning new languages really fun and easy. It allows you to schedule notifications so that you always get reminders when you need them. if you make a typo when answering, it recognizes it and doesn't count it as wrong. It lets you practice saying the words so you can work on getting your pronunciation correct. Most importantly, it focuses on teaching you to speak the new language as if it were your native language rather than teaching you to translate it to your native language.","2023-07",168,"+short,+fun,+listen,+lockp"],[5,"So i haven't been diligently practicing my lessons but since I've learned some of the basics from prior Spanish classes, high school, and the fact that I work with a lot of Spanish speakers, it is definitely a great refresher on pronunciation and terminology. The formal and informal has always been hard for me as well as \"me\" and \"you\" so being able to go back and correct which is which in a review is a big help. Other language courses just threw you in and didn't have the versatility this does","2021-12",166,"+effect,+review,+listen,+exam"],[1,"Super predatory payment structure. Can't unsubscribe from inside the app, have to hunt around on the website. If you get billed, can't cancel before the next payment cycle (yearly) without losing your profile, data etc so \"sunk cost remorse\". Basically relies on people forgetting to cancel after the trial, auto-billing 80 bucks(!) then \"might as well use it for a year, then cancel\"... forget to do so and get billed again, etc. It's a fine language app but it's so scammy I'm too annoyed to use it","2023-05",164,"pay"],[4,"I overall like the app, but the keyboard is very difficult to use and is lacking in symbols, so I am unable to type things like \"dix-neuf\" and get marked wrong, which is out of my control. The speaking function is very useful, but it only works if the area is completely quiet, so I wish there were an option to skip or delay it for when I am not in a quiet environment. It would also be more useful if it could tell me how close or off I am from proper pronunciation.","2020-03",164,"+listen,+wish"],[3,"Latest update is frustrating. I always do the daily practice, which is sometimes 5 exercises, sometimes 50+. The Practice icon had a little number bubble that said the number of items to do that day. This number is gone now and just a red dot. Why remove the count? Update: Thank you for removing the practice animation that popped up halfway through the lesson.","2025-09",160,"+habit"],[3,"The app is quite buggy. Does not work as described. You cannot navigate forward or backward inside any lesson. If you wish to repeat a page you cannot except to repeat the entire lesson. I've already found errors in the language structure and rules. For example the use of masculine and feminine a vs o at the end of a word. The training tells you one thing then the examples to it differently. Speech recognition system doesn't work. Get stuck if you try to practice speaking. Must exit app to reset","2022-02",160,"bug,data,voice,repeat,wish,+exam,+wish"],[4,"Many good features. It marks it wrong if you don't put an accent over a letter but most keyboards don't have accents. Doesn't always hear me when I pronounce correctly. I feel the pace of the course is too quick for older learners. Especially the part where you have to listen to 2 people have an entire conversation. Also when something is wrong there's a discouraging red highlight & loud noise. After filling in blanks the page disappears so we can't see the correct answer for more than 1 second.","2022-04",157,"+short,+listen"],[5,"Recently, when reviewing vocabulary, it only uses words from the last couple of lessons. Where did all the vocabulary go? I like to do a new lesson each day, and then review vocabulary, randomly selected from day 1 of my lessons. The old vocabulary is there any longer! If this is not fixed, I will néed to use a new app. I need to review old vocabulary so it doesn't get forgotten and refreshes my memory. The app is ineffective if I only can review words from the last few lessons 😡 (Fixed)","2024-09",156,"+effect,+review"],[4,"Absolutely love the reminders, courses, and ease of use. I wish the speech recognition of \"v\" was better. I wish the directions for a few of the activities were just a tad bit more clear. And I especially wish I could go in and review all the things I have learned and it gave me options to just shuffle review them. Overall absolutely amazing and would highly recommend.","2020-05",152,"+effect,+review,+lockp,+wish"],[4,"I have added an additional star from my previous review because the app had addressed the issue that caused me to rage quit it the first time: when you play a pronunciation back multiple times, the pronunciation slows down. This is an appreciated improvement, but it would be nice if there was a way to more precisely control that speed, like with YouTube. The app does not seem to support Spanish to English, or at least it's not intuitive on how to configure that.","2023-04",149,"+review,+listen,+wish"],[4,"A solid language learning app. I like that it teaches you specific grammatical rules as it goes along and that it isn't too gamey. It has a major flaw though. Its speech recognition is bad. Normally it works okay but there are some words it just can't seem to identify. Also whenever it detects something wrong it gives you these little messages like \"keep trying mistakes are important for learning\" and I find them very irritating and patronizing when the speech recognition is what is failing","2022-12",143,"+fun"],[4,"Great tool for learning the basics and some more advanced structures to grammar for different languages. Generally it's been a pleasant process for me, I'm learning Spanish in my down time at work. However, the voice detection is kinda buggy, and really gets me a bit agitated at times, where I'll repeat a complex statement and it picks up my pronunciation just fine, then all of a sudden it won't recognize the word \"Sí\". Then I feel either forced to turn off the mic, or restart the app.","2021-06",141,"+listen"],[3,"I like many aspects of this app but the speaking component is terrible. At first I thought I was a bad speaker because everything was marked incorrect, but then I got my partner to try (native speaker) and she was also marked incorrect for nearly everything. I'm talking simple words like \"pom\". That's not good enough for a paid language learning app. Also there are far too many repetitive elements of lessons, like spelling the exact same phrase ad nauseam until it just feels like a chore.","2025-02",139,"ad,wrong,repeat,+short"],[4,"So far so good. In terms of teching everyday conversation quickly, its great. However, I feel like the need to repeat the words/phrases into the microphone to progress in the lesson is unnecessary. Especially when half the time IT DOESN'T WORK. It just doesn't register that you've said anthing and you can't skip it. It's nice to practice pronunciation but at least throw in a skip button until the issue with voice recognition is fixed","2020-07",139,"+short,+listen"],[4,"It's a fine app I like how they place emphasis on learning real life phrases, and unlike Duolingo, the voices you listen to sound way more human It's just the speech feature which is frustrating. If you have a short word you're outta luck. Sometimes it doesn't even register me speaking. I could say the same sentence, the same way and it would mark me incorrect the first time, correct the second. I find the best way for it to pick you up is to speak unnaturally slow. Which defeats the purpose","2024-01",138,"+short"],[3,"The lessons are great. It helps you progress at a good pace without overwhelming you. I used it for 6 months before a trip to Italy and was able to speak well enough to make due. Only 3 stars because the app is extremely buggy. It crashes constantly often in the middle of lessons. As others have mentioned, the voice recognition doesn't work at all so the Speaking Lessons are totally useless. It's been like this for years so it doesn't seem like the company has any intention of fixing these bugs.","2024-05",129,"bug,voice,+effect"],[2,"Not terrible, but it has more negatives than positives. Voice recognition isn't great. Can't move between different languages like other free options. Lessons keep getting longer so it is difficult to do bite sized lessons. Focus seems to be more on cultural sites and less about the actual language. I will not renew my subscription when the time comes","2023-01",127,"pay,voice"],[5,"I've been messing around with the apps interface, and it has been easy to naviagte and quite responsive. Everything is layed out well, (as in being easy to understand) and the connectivity is seemless. Sadly in my case, Japanese, the language I was interested in working on is not offered. Other than that personal dissapointment, the app is great! It should help anyone who is interested in learning any of the provided languages.","2020-06",127,"+short"],[5,"I'm enjoying the app. I like the various ways it gets you to learn the words and to speak. For someone who is advanced in a language, I'm still trying to find the advanced lessons. I did find advanced podcasts so that's good. UPDATE: Great customer service. I changed to the Castilian Spanish and the advanced lessons are there. I studied linguistics and just love how Babbel is set up to easily and completely teach language.","2022-07",125,"+fun,+custom"],[4,"I really love this app. It helps you feel like you are learning and making progress right away. There's a great mix of conversations, culture, vocab, and grammar. My biggest complaint is that the speech recognition on mobile is absolutely atrocious. I refuse to use Babbel on mobile for this reason because I cannot progress the lesson without incorrect errors. I only use this on my computer and it's much better. I also wish I could see the literal translation for each line during the lessons.","2022-08",121,"+effect,+wish"],[4,"Love this! It's not competitive like Duolingo, and it's lobly focused on your learning, which you can do in numerous ways! It has so many activities, games, and cultural information. It provides context to what you learn as well! My only complaint is the self-report of your progress, I feel like a mini test or something as a measure with a line graph might be better.","2024-04",115,"+fun,+exam"],[4,"overall, this is a good tool for learning languages. after about a month of 30-minute daily sessions, I can form basic sentences on my own. as with other language apps, there isn't any variation in review questions so it doesn't force you to apply your learnings. there are a number of ways for you to access content which can lead you to stray from the structured - not a bad thing. the speech recognition will often show that I'm saying exactly what I'm supposed to but still mark it incorrect.","2020-08",112,"+review,+habit"],[2,"Not a serious opportunity for trial. I wanted to try this app as a replacement for the silly exercises in Duolingo. I chose that I was a mid level learner, but my first and only example lesson was about \"hello\" and \"goodbye.\" Beginner level lesson that didn't let me really see how it works. Not interested in a subscription for an app I can't properly try first, and it wasn't worth my time to try it.","2023-04",110,"pay"],[1,"I initially was very much impressed with the Program and the customer service technician. However for the last number of weeks I have submitted numerous emails regarding a significant problem. I followed the instructions exactly, with O results. I don't get it. You are supposed to be one if not the Best. Well in my opinion means resolving issues if your algorithms error. Now after diligent effort to learn through your program has ceased. It's extremely frustrating when you can get Help !!!","2022-09",109,"bug,cs"],[5,"Loving the app. Don't expect it to replace a tutor, or formal classes. That said, it does what it does extremely well so far, covering the important basics first, and repeatedly for reinforcement. I did get the subscription for a reasonable cost, use it every day, and although I need to study a bit off on the side, the app meets all reasonable expectations. Thanks devs, well done 🙂","2020-09",109,"+exam,+habit"],[1,"I lowered the rating. I REALLY dont care for this software. I don't feel like I'm learning anything. There's not enough repetition for words to stick. It dumps a bunch of grammar rules all at once. Often, you have the sentence with no translation. When you do a review, it covers a word you've seen maybe twice over a week ago. I was hoping that this might give some more formal training compared to duolingo, but it hasn't. Extremely disappointed and wishing I could get my money back.","2025-01",108,"pay,lack"],[1,"Voice recognition is real bad. Lessons are decent but it's all over the place in some areas. Does a okay job at reading but when it comes to writing and speaking it's not a good experience. Spend the extra money and just take an actual class. Update - impossible to speak as lessons teach you sentences. They throw words at you in the sentence you've never practiced so trying to speak a full sentence without knowing the word first. First lessons were great, then it turns into a mess quickly.","2023-05",107,"pay,voice"],[2,"This would be a good program if, when, you began having trouble with the language, it would recommend you retake sections or at least give you the option. if you have trouble during a section it lets you correct the errors, but if you only have so much time and you really don't understand what you messed up, you could spend hours in one sitting on one section. it should also quit having popups that explain something with the only option being \"Got it.\" it needs a \"Don't got it\" option.","2019-08",107,"bug,lock"],[2,"If you can find a discount price (I got a lifetime subscription for substantially less) then it's worth it. The content itself is definitely working and feels more robust and useful than Duolingo. Just don't waste your time tracking activities or streaks. The app is at best buggy and it rarely acknowledges either on a consistent basis. (And \"tech support\" is laughably bad. They couldn't care less.) But still worth the price if you can find it on sale. Update 6/30/24. Support remains useless.","2024-07",107,"pay,bug"],[2,"A major rip-off that's ONLY usable by absolute beginners. Even if you pay for the insanely expensive lifetime license, you can't even get to upper-beginner without paying AGAIN for individual live courses. $300 and you literally won't even touch on past-tense. It seems like the entire app is structured around getting as much money from you as fast as possible, with the assumption that you'll give up (which most people do) before you realize you've been ripped off.","2024-01",105,"pay,bug"],[3,"I used the website version years ago and liked it, but I paid for 6 months on the app and I'm not really liking it at all. The voice recorder doesn't seem to hear me half the time, but the real issue is with the keyboard. If I'm supposed to be using different punctuation for you to accept the answer, it shouldn't be nearly impossible to FIND said punctuation in the keyboard (or accents for that matter). I also couldn't find how to test out of all the beginner lessons, so am having to go again.","2022-04",103,"+listen,+exam"],[4,"I like this app relearning French to move up in my work place (tried Spanish but i can't roll the 'R'). However I do have a slight speech impediment and have a hard time saying some words. Very frustrating and discouraging when I try to say words through the mic. I get \"try again\" multiple times (that's why the 4☆). I understand that some words misspoken can mean different things. So I don't do the speak part anymore just listen and games. Other than that, I really enjoy this.","2022-06",103,"+fun"],[4,"The course seems to be well paced and teach useful information and phrases. I have a few critiques of the app itself though. The font is very small and there doesn't seem to be a way of accessing grammar rules and verb conjugations for review. As it is I just use other websites as a support. Also the input keyboard could be better designed. Typing numbers and accented letters is tedious. There are a few other glitches but generally it's a decent course.","2020-07",103,"+review,+listen"],[2,"I didn't get any free trial. Just nought a month before even trying the app. The flow for apps like these are always imperfect and clunky. I wish you could choose just audio practice or full immersion instead of being spoon fed no matter what you choose. Please help me cancel my payment for this month I just saw there are in fact advanced zoom classes available ie \"immersion\" but I would have to pay extra for 3+ on top of the membership fees???? What in the fresh hell.","2023-03",101,"pay,wish"],[1,"It's the best language app I've looked at as far as teaching in a useful order. This will probably get you conversational faster than any of the others, but the interface is horrible. 1) They sometimes give you a partial keyboard with letters scrambled. It's more a game to unscramble the letters than to actually learn the words. I just want to type them. Words that I forgot, and wouldn't have gotten the answer, I just unscrambled the letters. 2) I entered a sentence with the pronoun \"Yo aprendo espanol\". It told me I was wrong because it wanted \"Aprendo espanol\". They are both correct. The program is wrong. 3) On lines with more than one field to enter, you have to enter one, hit done, then enter the next, and so on. The process is slow and annoying. I should be able to tap the next field, enter the answer, then tap \"Done\" when I'm done. 4) The program is very slow to respond. (Which makes item 3 and item 5 SO much worse.) 5) The button that says \"done\" when you are ready, shows \"Show answer\" when the field is empty. I have accidentally hit the button a number of times because I was trying to hit the \"Done\" button again (figuring I missed it because the program is SO slow). It then fills in the answer and tells me I'm wrong. When the field is blank before I enter my answer the first time, the button shouldn't do anything. It should say \"show answer\" only after I've made a mistake. As I said, the content is excellent, but the interface is too frustrating for me to deal with. I have a trial period. I will be ending before I pay. If they offer a trial to you, it might be worth trying, but I hated it.","2020-07",100,"pay,bug,wrong,ui"],[1,"\"Be aware \" this app might have good content, but they don't offer as many courses as advertised, and their customer service is the worst. I subscribed to the 1 year membership, and everything was going fine until I got to the intermidate B2 level in french. then the app pushed me back to a refresher course I don't need. I contacted the babbel team by email and phone, explaining to them that I don't have access to the B2 level. However, it's been a week without any reply.","2023-09",95,"pay,ad,cs"],[4,"Great so far! I am relearning French after many years out from high school. I really like the interactive app platform with combinations of listening, speaking, and typing. My only complaint is that the beginner dialogs with native speakers are sometimes way too fast to hear and comprehend. I can only tell what they are saying by looking at the English translations, which doesn't give me the benefit of understanding the spoken dialect. Save the fast speaking for advanced courses.","2022-05",93,"+listen,+exam"],[5,"It's great. However, there are times when they ask us to answer questions BEFORE they've taught the vocab and/or grammar to us and that throws me off a little bit. Also, I don't like how it progresses to the next screen automatically. I want to study what I am learning and have a moment to reflect on what the final answer is. The lessons themselves are actually helpful and I retain a lot of information.","2026-01",93,"+effect"],[1,"Literally unusable. The mic activities are mandatory, but it can't tell when something has been said regardless of the mic sensitivity setting. There's no way to manually indicate it should stop recording, so it just keeps recording until the 2 minute limit, and forces you to\"try\" twice. Lessons can't be skipped, so it's a mandatory 16-20 minutes of starting 8-10 failed recordings so you can move past the lesson with everything failed.","2022-10",92,"voice"],[4,"One of the better language learning software's. My one gripe with it is that it is not free although free learning and applications are on the rise. However, when compared to other software learning apps, this one is much more engaging and can become more difficult in a good way. As a Spanish speaker I am able to further my knowledge of the language with this app while free apps like duolingo are far too easy for me.","2020-05",90,"+short,+free"],[5,"This is hands down the best app for learning a new language. I have tried nearly every app for learning a language, and IMO, Babbel is the best one around. It has focused lessons on every aspect of reading, writing, and speaking a language. It implements not only repetition to learn, but focus on key points like grammar. They have games to make memorization fun, podcasts for learners on the go, and free one on one classes. The only thing I wish it had was a competitive aspect like duolingo has.","2023-03",90,"+effect,+review,+fun,+exam,+free,+wish"],[5,"I've been using this app for over a year now and like it a lot. One of the differentiators versus other language apps that made me stick with it is the amount of vocab. I'm generally good with grammar at this point, but so many words I want to know. One improvement I'd like to see is the ability to tag words you definitely know very well - the review section has gotten unmanageable now that it has 1800 words in it, and I'm 100% sure I don't need to practice certain super basic things anymore.","2024-03",90,"+review,+wish"],[5,"Babbel is like the more formal version of Duolingo. The courses are easy to do yet informative, although I wish they offered more options like Hangul. But my favorite feature is that you can do a one-time purchase valid for 99 years. That's right, a LIFETIME LICENSE- IN 2025! I'm sure others are also sick of subscriptions and just want to buy a product once, so it's very refreshing to hear companies say \"look, just give us the cash now, you won't have to worry about payments again.\"","2025-01",88,"+short,+wish"],[5,"Fantastic tool for learning languages. I am currently learning French and Italian and it helps a lot. The review options let you practice in different ways, letting you focus on things you may need more practice with. You can also choose how to to approach your lessons. Overall a great app, the reminders are also a great way to remember to do your lessons.","2021-06",88,"+effect,+review,+lockp"],[4,"I do love the app so far. I've had it almost a year. But the one thing I wish they would do is allow you to unmark lessons as done. I get busy different times of the year and don't use the app for a while. When I get back into it, I like to redo lessons as a good refresher. It would be much easier to remember where I left off on older completed lessons if I could uncheck them as done. Other than that though, I'm very much enjoying the app.","2020-09",87,"+effect,+fun,+wish"],[5,"I just got a lifetime subscription with access to all of the 15 languages. I started with Portuguese and I love it so far! It is fun and easy to use and there is repetition, voice.. I like that the lessons are short and you can do them even on a busy schedule. I like the emphasis on spoken language. I recommend for beginners interested in learning a new language.","2020-04",80,"+short,+review,+fun"],[1,"Speech recognition is awful. I'd say it was only on my device (Pixel 7a) but after reading the other reviews it seems more widespread than that. Really doesn't help that I have to press the microphone between 2 and 6 times to get it to register (which really doesn't help with the frustration of trying to get it to hear me). Unfortunately I bought a year so I just had to disable speaking exercises so I could move on without that experience.","2024-06",79,"voice"],[1,"Can't cancel subscription. Signed up once and paid $24.95 for an annual pass and quickly became bored and didn't use app past the first 4 days. Just got a notice that it charged me $24.95 again (2 months after annual purchase) and there is no way to cancel on app etc. Currently jumping through hoops trying to get a refund for the 2nd unauthorized payment. Can't get a response from Babbel.","2021-11",78,"pay"],[5,"Got it when I decided to better myself by learning a new language. I like the layout and easy to use format of the app. The lessons progress at a decent rate allowing you to fully grasp the content before moving on. It also allows you to review it at any time in different ways. You can learn to not only speak the languages but read and write in them pretty decently too. The lessons aren't long so you can squeeze on in anywhere. Definitely reccommend for anyone of any age wanting to learn.","2023-01",76,"+short,+review"],[2,"There is truly very little German content, making the long subscriptions borderline fraudulent. The more advanced lessons are shorter and of lower quality, both the recordings and the exercises. The app has no dark mode, so it’s not so pleasant to use at night. Overall, I recommend against this app. It's better than Duolingo and even a bit better than Busuu, but I still think most people would learn faster elsewhere. Again, I strongly advise against long subscriptions.","2022-08",75,"pay"],[5,"Update: This was fixed within a week or so. Thank you! I find the grammar lessons to be really helpful, and that's probably what I like most about the app. ............ Prior review here: Was completing the British English to German course, and lost all my progress in the app. When I load the app, all my course progress is gone. This is not acceptable, but I will update my review if this gets resolved.","2024-07",75,"+effect,+review"],[5,"I enjoy the varied types of practice, like speaking, spelling, listening and reading because I want to improve them all. It does a good job of gradually increasing the difficulty such as using pictures at the beginning to aid memory making. It schedules review to help me retain what I've learned & levels each word or phrase based on how often I get it wrong to give me the right amount of repeated practice. I knew a little Spanish before starting this app but I certainly know more after 3 weeks!","2022-11",74,"+effect,+review,+fun,+listen,+wish"],[1,"It goes on and on with phrases then grammar of irregular verbs without the ability to enter phrases you would like to say and hear the pronunciation and see the spelling. For example, soft butter,... Beurre doux. Deux vs. Doux. I could go on with many examples, but you get the idea. Just another company that wants to own you as long as possible, rather than build a loyalty based on function provided. Now, I have to find out how to cancel and let the time run out. Not available in PROFILE.","2022-05",69,"voice"],[2,"Wasn't happy with Duolingo so thought I would try this. The sample lesson is one of the most basic lessons even though I said I already knew some Spanish. Doesn't seem to be a way to change that to sample a more difficult level. I'm uninsalling the app. I do like that they don't share info with 3rd parties. I don't like they collect data for advertising. I thought if you were paying there would be no ads.","2023-07",69,"pay,ad"],[3,"I like this app better than Duolingo. There's zero gamification or extortion, just solid lessons in a good format. I will probably subscribe to the app. HOWEVER. There is an issue with the speaking exercises, especially with monosyllabic words (many languages), it doesn't register them. Based on numerous posts on reddit, this issue has been around and unfixed for years. It's frustrating, as speaking is a large part of practicing a language. So I'm giving the app 3 stars for stressing me out.","2026-02",69,"pay"],[5,"Easy to understand. It uses repetition in different ways. I literally have random Spanish words going through my head. I understand a lot more and it has only been 9 months of learning, here and there, as I have the time. It uses different voices so that you become more familiar to actual people, rather than a computer enunciating every word. The app understands you pretty well in pronouncing each of your words. It has you do reviews in 10 question blocks, in case you only have a few minutes.","2021-01",68,"+short,+review"],[3,"I like being able to choose between different methods when practicing vocabulary - for example, I'm able to focus on pronunciation, if I want. This app's voice recognition, however, needs work. It sometimes marks me incorrect when I pronounce words correctly, and has also marked me correct when I make mistakes. Simpler graphics are more appealing, and Babbel does list the available languages for buyers to check before buying. If Japanese and Mandarin are in production, I look forward to those.","2020-08",67,"wrong,voice,+short,+listen,+exam"],[1,"WAAAAAAY too expensive and only the very first course is free! What are you thinking?? There's way too many better apps and websites that are free to be charging that much! On top of that, when I try to delete my account it just pops up with a dialog box that asks \"do you want to delete your account?\" and gives instructions but doesn't have any option to actually click anything or confirm anything to delete it. I guess I'm just stuck with an account that I can't delete for a worthless app.","2024-03",65,"pay,bug,data"],[3,"I like the lessons but lately can't get passed newcomer lesson 10 in Russian. I get ½-way thru & a popup gives me a rule. There's no way to close the screen so I can't proceed. The only option is to close the lesson which does allow me to continue where I left off but the same thing happens repeatedly. Very frustrating. Not motivating at all. Now, there's a break in my streak even tho I've practiced the same things repeatedly for over an hour. Very glitchy for the price. Disappointed. Pls fix.","2023-01",63,"pay,bug,lock,repeat,+fun,+habit"],[2,"It's okay at reinforcing what I knew but I didn't find it useful to really learn the language. Also, be aware they make it as difficult as they can to turn off auto renewal which is automatically turned on when you sign up. You have to cancel your subscription in a browser and lose access even if you had just paid. They won't allow you to simply toggle off auto renewal.","2023-07",61,"pay,bug"],[3,"Was really good for a year or so. It does a much better job at explaining certain things than most other apps. But for the past three months the microphone has just been messing up. My voice answers take forever to register, and it causes the lessons to take 4 times longer, just because of the loading. And that's if it actually works. Not a phone issue either, my phone mic works everywhere else. Hoping for a fix soon. I liked the lessons because they were quick, but now they take forever.","2024-04",61,"bug,voice,+short"],[4,"Excellent app for regular usage. I like the reviews and the clear explanations of grammar. Two suggestions: 1) Typing foreign language words by selecting from available letters is very annoying and not an effective way to practice new vocabulary. Filling in the blanks should allow for simple text entry instead. 2) I wish there were a better way to track overall progress, preferably through exams but even a points system could be useful. Great app overall!","2021-03",61,"+effect,+short,+review,+exam,+wish"],[4,"It's great, until the microphone needs to be used. Although usually works fine, there are times where the mic will not accept the correct pronunciation, and worse than that, occasionally the microphone will never leave the \"listening for answer to be finished\" state! I have had many times where I cannot finish a lesson because the microphone never stops, meaning that the question is never passed nor failed, which means the lesson can never progress! I believe this may be exclusive to Android.","2022-06",60,"+listen"],[5,"I needed to learn Spanish for my career, I am on lesson 6 of the introduction. It's very easy to learn the way each lesson is set up. There's about 8 additional classes with 7-10 lessons in each class. Lots to learn, I appreciate how easy it is to use, and I am learning at an improved pace at my own discretion. I love this app, and Babbel has done a great job, I look forward to learning another language in the future as well. 👍👍","2023-07",59,"+effect,+short,+exam,+wish"],[1,"Not optimal. I took advantage of the Black Friday sale last year. It's not the most straightforward with lesson plans, something I have to say Duolingo actually did better on (at least as of a few years ago when I used that app). This is just a muddle your way through with no direction, which is ridiculous for the price you're paying to use it. Also a reminder notice for renewal would be nice so I could've cancelled BEFORE paying that chunk again.","2025-12",58,"pay,wish"],[1,"URGENT: Do not download or purchase babbel. This was the worst software I've used. It is 100% a \"cookie cutter\" business model. Learning is not engaging, and they will not issue refunds. Use duo lingo, preply (real tutors affordable prices), AI tutors, or any other product other than this. I am very disappointed that I paid for this. Again, save yourself the trouble and do not purchase this program. There are much better options available, including duo lingo.","2023-10",58,"pay"],[4,"I'm stacking up a solid streak, but the voice recognition software needs improvement. It can be very discouraging to accept an imperfect score due to this widely reported technical issue, and it's the only thing standing in the way of a 5 star review. I am a big fan especially of the different options for reviewing vocab. I always choose the written option because I am hoping to work with Spanish speaking customers in a remote work environment.","2024-11",58,"+review,+fun,+habit,+custom,+wish"],[2,"For the most part, this app is good. I do like this style of learning more than other language apps. There is a benefit where this gives more explanation as to the intricacies of certain rules in the language, which makes it more helpful to retain and apply. However, this is not cheap and for a subscription based app, it's tremendously disappointing how bad the speaking exercises are. I've contacted Babbel support and there's no explanation or helpful tips to make it work better.","2022-06",57,"pay,cs"],[5,"I love the app. I particularly like how it explains grammatical concepts as they come up in dialogues and practice sentences. I also love how they sneak in extra vocab in the dialogues that they don't quiz you on. What I like to do is write down all the extra vocab that comes up, then make cards in Anki and tack that on to my review process. My one complaint is that I wish they had more languages! Seriously, if you guys get Hungarian, Japanese and Chinese on there, you can take all my money!","2021-11",57,"+review,+wish"],[1,"They only gloss over sentence structure and that's the meat of languages. And, you need to be VERY well versed in English grammar rules and terms or you won't even understand what they're talking about. I'm very sorry now that I paid for a lifetime subscription. Plus, each exercise is agonizingly slow. You type in the answer and have to wait, you go to the next item and you have to wait, etc. Update: I tried again and it's still absolutely horrible.","2024-05",55,"pay,bug"],[1,"Just bought a subscription and both app and website have had problems in the first day. First, I haven't been able to log in to the app at all. It keeps telling me it's for registered users only - but I can login with my email and password just fine in my browser. Second, I tried both Chrome and Edge on the website but the website doesn't work on fill in the blank exercises. You can't type anywhere except the first blank so it's impossible to finish. Glad I'm still in refund window. Updated: I had already contacted support when the developer commented. Support suggested things like signing in and out and that I should use Chrome or Edge, which were things I already said (in the email they responded to!) I tried and are already on Babbel's website as suggestions. I can't even rate if the method is good to learn a language from because this app was so nonfunctional. You only have a 20-day window for a refund (which I got successfully) so it's not like you have tons of time to go back and forth with support and wait it out till they get it together. Voice recognition is also atrocious, they should just get rid of it if it's not going to be useful. It's not even like there's just one bug that needs fixing on this app, it's so many things. I'm 90% sure there's no free trial option because no one would pay for this if they got to try it for a week first and they know so many people won't read or bother to email support for a refund.","2021-05",55,"pay,bug,data,voice,cs"],[1,"I am a beginner/intermediate and wanted to try something new. Unfortunately, I did not find the format of the lessons to my liking, and couldn't find an underlying structure to the lessons. This is just personal preference, but I also found the mobile app very, very slow and the desktop version couldn't pick up my voice, despite checking mic function. After 2 days, I requested a refund. It's now been 2 weeks and I can't get a response. I've found the process very frustrating.","2020-05",54,"pay,bug,voice"],[1,"It's really unfortunate this app can't eliminate the annoying chime sounds. You get chimed to death. It's loud. It's has to be loud so you can hear the rest of the app. Supposedly you can choose to turn off the teeth-grating pings but I've tried. Daily. Due to a supposed \"fix\" released 7/3/23. I really liked everything else about this app but it's a full stop. Now I just want my money back.","2023-07",54,"pay,ui"],[2,"It's really limited. You can only do ONE language on here, so if you want another language as well, you have to uninstall the app and reinstall and use another e-mail to register. I was hoping to learn 2, but it only shows up as one language available after I already registerd. It's nice to hear the words in sentences instead of just 1 person saying a word and someone else translating it. Could've, should've made the app more fun, so we could memorize it faster.","2021-08",54,"lack"],[1,"overpriced/cancelled: The exercises are poorly structured, the topics are not practical; there is no ability to click on words for the translation; difficult to keep up with the required learning pace; there are no pronounciation prules. I took a long break, after the restart the exercises were where I left, but I didn't remember any of them. There is no option to customize the learning pace. The UI is confusing and unfriendly. Subscription was purchased thru G store, but not shown there.","2025-08",51,"pay,ui"],[4,"Pretty good app, but the voice recognition can be off. In German, es and ihn are not hard. But for some reason, no matter how much I try, it will not give me a green check mark. I'm only perhaps two weeks in, but it makes me nervous how it is going to perform further in. The grammar rules are nice. I hope they continue to develop them. There is a nice mix of speaking, reading, grammar, and vocab building.","2025-03",51,"+wish"],[5,"I greatly prefer this method of learning where grammar is part of the learning process instead of trying to sort out why parts of speech are in a specific order. I find the incorporation of speaking, spelling and selecting the option to be well balanced and most suitable to my learning style. I used another, game like, language tool that was helpful, but was not meeting my learning needs. I have progressed much faster in my goal of becoming fluent in another language with Babbel..","2025-06",51,"+effect,+fun"],[3,"Content-wise it is much better than Duolingo that I tried first. It actually explains things and does so in a logical order. However, it is missing some polish. There are little things like not showing how many words are needed for a text entry field, pages with more than 4 vocab words with pictures being too big to fit on one screen. Edit: it lost another star because there's no way to find where you learned something before and go back and do it again to review.","2024-10",50,"+effect,+review"],[4,"I've been using another product for several years and I like it, but I needed more practice speaking. In a couple of weeks, I've learned several more common vocabulary words, and have a better understanding of some concepts. I wish the keypad in the app on my mobile device was more like the built-in keyboard. Sometimes typing can be error-prone with the in-app keyboard.","2022-09",50,"+effect,+wish"],[5,"I was terrible at learning Spanish in high school. I have been studying German for a few months with Babbel. It is going well. It is enjoyable and fun. I find it very helpful that I can start and stop a session to suit my needs. I study multiple times a day for short periods. When I reach a point where it is tiresome I stop. Then later in the day I enjoy another session until I find it tiresome. The Babbel app allows me the freedom to learn in this peculiar method that works for me.","2025-02",50,"+effect,+short,+fun,+exam"],[1,"In my opinion I think that Duolingo is better because it's laid out more neatly. It's much more bright and colorful. The accent marks and pronunciation are better. I really like how it's broken into categories you can choose like family, phrases, food, school, work, and, recreation. Even simple ones like colors, shapes, and numbers. I know this might sound like it's an | •ad | but I don't work for them I'm just giving you helpful suggestions 😉.","2020-01",49,"ad,bug,voice"],[5,"I love this app. The different ways they help you learn are really interactive, from flashcards and spelling to speaking and listening. I can repeat as many lessons as I want or need to and the encouraging prompts when you get it wrong, make you wanna keep learning. There are little bits of information scattered throughout lessons and it definitely doesn't feel like learning from a book. They really have a lot to offer if you wanna learn a new language!","2020-09",49,"+review,+listen"],[1,"I wish there was so much more engaging and accessible practice than what babble provides. I find myself using Duolingo so much more because the practice it offers, I actually end up learning and absorbing so much more. I'm so bummed I paid for this when there are many awesome free options out there. I really tried with this app. But I just don't WANT to use it. I kind of dread going on it. Honestly aside from the lack of practice, it's also just really boring.","2022-12",48,"repeat,wish"],[3,"The lessons are well thought out and effective. I would like to follow my friends' progress, because that makes learning more fun. Add that and this is an easy 4 stars. I'm not sure what's going on, but when I look at the \"how are you\" badge in achievements, it shows that the section has been completed, but when I click on it, it says that I've only completed 1 of 9 lessons. I've definitely completed all 9. Similar with other achievements.","2024-03",47,"+effect,+short,+fun"],[5,"It helps to learn a new language, and it's very easy to use, but if you want to learn more than hello than you have to pay for the services. It costs like 12 dollars for a month and goes up to like 8 months, it's not much and the app works really well, it repeats everything multiple times and goes over spelling and teaches you about the language you're learning. If you're thinking about getting this app and you're willing to pay for it then you should definitely get it. Seriously","2018-09",47,"+effect,+short"],[3,"I'm really enjoying this and can't wait to get more in-depth. This is a refresher for me. My French has gotten quite rusty. One slight criticism is that the app seems to mark some of my recordings as incorrect at random times. Yesterday, literally everyone was marked as being wrong, but today, they are all correct. At least this isn't being graded. Adding: I wish there was a way to just bypass the recording portions. It just isn't reliable, at all. Otherwise, a good program.","2024-04",46,"wrong,wish,+fun,+wish"],[1,"I had to buy a subscription to check out the app. No problem, given what they advertised, it appeared that this would be good for me as an advanced Spanish language learner looking to brush up on vocab. I subscribed, logged in, and absolutely nothing. All beginner courses, some intermediate, no advanced. I canceled the subscription immediately. If you want to learn past beginner status, stick with lingodeer or the owl. Edit: received refund. Babbel support confirmed no advanced courses.","2024-06",45,"pay,ad"],[1,"Doesn't have Japanese, barely has any support for Brazilian Portuguese. The course is incredibly small. Live costs your soul. There is no AI conversation partner, guided conversations, grammar guide, or audio recap for Brazilian Portuguese. I was more than willing to pay for the 3 monthly sub and even the lifetime subscription until I realized how short this course actually is and that there is no Japanese course. I can't find it worth it now. edit: my issue is not the number of languages.","2025-04",44,"pay"],[2,"The courses cover a lot of great material. But the speech recognition is absolutely awful compared to other apps. It marks almost ALL speech incorrect when I'm certain my pronunciation is correct sometimes. Modifying the mic sensitivity does not help at all. This drawback is not useful and is very discouraging when trying to learn to speak a new language. Probably wont renew my monthly subscription if this continues. Glad I didn't pay for yearly.","2020-10",44,"pay,bug,wrong,voice"],[1,"Not a big fan. I unfortunately purchased the membership before trying it. It felt like it was moving too fast with some important words and too slow with some very useless worlds. As an example, I dont need to know how to spell Italian, spanish and German but that seems to be the emphasis in the first few lessons. And since the quizzes are so picky with the spelling it takes a long time for me to get through it. I really wish they would focus more on common words you need in order to communicate","2020-10",43,"bug,wish"],[5,"I love this app!! I'm having to learn Spanish for my job and the way they put the lessons together teaches you how to converse instead of just memorizing words. The best part though is when it's time to review the lesson they allow you to choose HOW you review... writing, flash cards, multiple choice or speaking. This app keeps your attention and makes in fun to learn!! THANK YOU BABBLE!!","2022-11",43,"+effect,+review,+fun"],[5,"I have enjoyed using Babble. I have (temporary) staff sent to me daily. Often they are struggling w English as their second or even sixth language! I suggest Babble, and a dictionary site that also has a lot more information on word use, thesaurus, more info on single words than I've seen in one place before. This gives them information and practice pronouncing, sentence structure, all that. Eventually, if they do some work on learning, it improves their skills for employment in the future.","2021-03",42,"+fun,+habit,+wish"],[4,"I like the app generally, but have a couple of issues. The first is that sometimes when I review a section, and it requires me to repeat a word, the word isn't always heard. This may be due to weak signal strength because of the location I happen to be at when doing the review. Another problem is that when I'm asked to spell a word, the keyboard doesn't have the option for selecting the Enya letter, just the standard English alphabet.","2022-04",41,"+review"],[1,"I tried the practice version, but it covered words I already knew. Paid for the regular version for three months but quickly realized it wasn't going to work for me. I quickly contacted the company (less than a week after purchase) about a refund but no response. Tried the program again since I couldn't get a refund but no success and simply became frustrated. I guess if you're over a certain age this program doesn't work and is a waste of money.","2021-04",40,"pay,bug,cs"],[4,"Good app for learning languages, it teaches the basics and principles better than Duolingo. I'm learning French, and the voice recognition has serious issues. I've literally tested some words with perfect pronunciation (not from me) and the app says it's pronounced wrong. Some words I've had to intentionally pronounce wrong to be detected. For example, when pronouncing the word \"sept\" (7), I have to pronounce the silent 'p' which is incorrect but the only way the app detects it.","2024-10",40,"+listen,+exam"],[5,"I have been working with several apps to learn languages and have found Babbel to be one of the more intuitive ones. The lessons are short enough that you can do a few each day if you want and each lesson uses several different techniques to help you learn the material. So far, at least through the Newcomer section, the explanations are clear. I definitely reccomend this app.","2020-05",40,"+short"],[4,"Only 4 starts because I've only been on the app for a little bit. But it seems to be a really great app. Would recommend **Edit. I think it would be a great idea to add a section where the user can say/ask what they'd like to learn. I was also trying to learn Spanish with a co-worker and I would have to keep asking how to say specific words or how to ask certain phrases. So I think adding a section to pick what you want to learn would be good too.","2019-11",38,""],[5,"Great app. User interface is awesome, lessons are set up in a way that is easy to learn and smooth to transition from one to another. Also for the price, the product is great. Awesome for killing time, beating boredom, or just expanding your knowledge. One thing the developers should fix though. When lesson require you to record yourself pronouncing words you can press record and then press the play button for the sample pronunciation and it will record the sample thus falsely passing you.","2021-07",38,"+short,+listen"],[3,"Good content, but UI is buggy. I like the explanations of grammar and phonetics and realistic conversations. The microphone button needs to be tapped several times to work. I cannot for the life of me get voice recognition to work for single syllable words. I thought I was just terrible at Swedish vowels (despite getting it right for longer phrases), but it seems other users have this issue. I expect a more polished experience for the price.","2024-12",37,"pay,bug,voice,ui"],[4,"I like this app more than Duolingo for learning. It teaches you grammar and rules, instead of just vocabulary. Main issues: 1. There are always issues launching the app. Almost every time I have to open the app twice 2. I don't like the activities where you unscramble individual letters to form words, would rather type the words directly with my keyboard 3. I would rather learn more things relative to travel and daily life instead of setting up picnics and random occupations","2025-02",36,"+habit"],[5,"I've been using Babble for many months, and I've learned very well! Some of my favorite things about Babbel include how the dialogue is very clear and every word is spoken clearly, the review center, and how you can make your own set of vocabulary words to study. I also like how there is a real life conversation in the end of most lessons, which I think helps me learn the most. Highly recommend this app to learn languages!","2024-07",36,"+effect,+review"],[2,"Decent interface but $15/ month per language is ridiculous. If it's going to be a subscription just let the customers learn as many languages as they want at once, or pay a one time fee per language. Furthermore, subject matter doesnt make sense for beginners. First I need to know the numbers, how, what, where, do you have..., etc. In 3 weeks I could count to 8 and say \"I work with 2 italians\". Hardly necessary vocab for a tourist. I'm going with a different app after my subscriptions are up.","2022-10",35,"pay,ui"],[2,"Overall, not great. I've been using this app on and off for a couple years and still can't really hold a conversation. my phone and app constantly have syncing issues where I try to maintain a long streak but the other device won't immediately sync. it's happening almost every single time now and I've reached out to support numerous times and they are completely unhelpful. they just told me to update my apps, which I did, and it still happens. if I could get a refund for my subscription, I would","2025-09",35,"pay,bug,data"],[5,"I like it much better than other apps because: 1. it forces you to remember things (they have their own keyboard, so you cannot cheat with the autocomplete). 2. They remind you of the new words at the right frequency for them to stick 3. There is a lot of grammar in it, so you understand why the sentence looks that way, instead of just learning it. Thing to improve: sometimes they dumb it down too much. Like the size of the space to fill leaves no doubt on what the answer is","2019-12",35,"+effect,+wish"],[1,"The learning path is unclear. The content jumps around a lot. Most of the lessons consist of writing the ends of words or selecting the written version of what is said out of a couple options. I don't think I learned anything. There aren't any fun aspects to help with enjoyability or motivation. The audio lessons had value for me but there were only a few and I can't figure out how to get more. Babbel Speak couldn't understand me, not even \"buenos dias.\" I don't know how this got good reviews.","2025-11",34,""],[1,"Simply too expensive and requires too much payment up front. Can they not have a free version with ads like many other apps do? Can they not allow you to pay it month by month instead of forcing you to pay for 3 months minimum all at once? Who in this day and age, in this economy, would spend so much money on an app after only one free lesson which is not really enough to judge?","2025-11",34,"pay,ad"],[2,"I have been using this service to learn Spanish for 3 months. At first, it was wonderful. I love the podcasts & some of the new interactive features like the AI conversations, but now I find it boring & difficult to keep up. It isn't engaging at all, & I'm not sure how I'm halfway through the second lesson plan when I don't understand 85% of the words I'm learning. The verbal tenses & word origins mean absolutely nothing to me if I can't understand what I'm reading or hearing. Expensive too","2025-04",34,"pay,repeat"],[1,"Recommending you do not download the app. There's not really a way to try it out without paying a subscription for it. And it's harder to cancel than a gym membership. It will automatically sign you up for a \"free trial\" that expires in 2 weeks and automatically charges your Google play - unless you go through multi-step process on their website, customer service, etc...","2025-03",33,"pay,cs"],[1,"I paid for a month and discontinued the renewal like after 2 weeks so I didn't forget because I wasn't taking another month. And they took away all of my services I couldn't get in anymore it was like I didn't pay in the first place. This is terrible, no way to claim this either. I tried with google services and they denied the refund as well. Super terrible. The app is okay but Duolingo is for free with some advertisements and you'll learn the same.","2023-12",33,"pay,ad"],[1,"Kind of disappointed. It focuses way too much on spelling and the format is slow, clumsy, and unnecessarily frustrating. I also don't like the listen and repeat format which often is very slow as well. I bought a 3 month subscription so I will keep plodding along and hope they make improvements. Never mind. I canceled my 53 plus dollar subscription and I wish I could get a full refund. What a horrible app. Completely useless and annoying. Pass that on to your developers jerks!!!!!","2024-09",33,"pay,bug,repeat,ui,wish"],[5,"I am enjoying using Babbel so far. It's very easy to navigate and I feel I am learning well with it in the first few lessons so far. The activities it uses to help you understand how to use each word really help to make it stick in my mind. I read other reviews how others were having trouble with the voice capturing part, but I have had no issues with it. I found that if you just tap the record icon and then pronounce the word with your phone far enough away from your mouth it will capture it.","2023-02",33,"+short,+review,+fun"],[1,"Terrible experience. Took my money for a six month subscription, allowed me to access one lesson in which I learned four words. When I tried to access lesson #2, they would not allow me access until I'd paid for a second six month subscription. So basically if you use this app you'll be paying hundreds of dollars to learn a minimal number of words. I'm currently trying to get my money back from them but am getting no answers. Total ripoff app.","2023-01",32,"pay"],[1,"You'd think an app that wants you to pay to learn a language would provide enough to get you started with something, like a series of lessons to get your feet wet, get you set up in a routine, and then entice you to pay. This app only gives you a single lesson ... and the lessons are EXTREMELY tiny. Part 1 of lesson 1 told me how to say my name. That's it. That's all I got for free. Not enough for me to know if i want to continue the language, not enough for me to decide if the app is worth it.","2021-07",32,"pay,lack"],[4,"Overall good! Engaging and practical. 1 star removed because of difficulty recording for the Speaking Practice sections. I have no delusions of my ability, but I'm not that bad at pronunciation but it's maddening to repeat the same phrase in my 'normal' voice repeatedly then fail repeatedly until I sort of bellow or something like an angry telenovela lead, which usually finally gets me a \"pass\". Maybe it's kinda funny, but I just skip those sections now.","2020-11",32,"+listen"],[5,"Lessons include reading writing (fill in the blank), listening and speaking. the beta feature where you can have a conversation with an AI \"person \" did not work on my galaxy s21. I used their tech support and they identified the problem quickly. They suggested reducing the size of my display font and the problem was solved. Excellent support.","2025-10",32,"+short,+listen"],[2,"Not a fan of the app and am now stuck since I paid for 3 months and can't figure out how to get a refund. I've had the app for about 3 days and half the time, all I get is a blank, white page when I open the app. I only have a certain amount of time daily to devote so I paid for an app with blank pages. Also, the voices seem off and don't pronounce all words correctly which is what I want to learn. Won't use again!","2022-10",31,"pay,bug"],[4,"Overall very good, but one improvement I would find very helpful would be an option to retake a language course without deleting all your vocabulary. I would like to keep my vocabulary progress, but retake the courses. I've been retaking the course manually, but it would be nice to have a \"retake course\" button without deleting everything. Voice recognition is sometimes finicky, but overall it is a very good app.","2026-08",31,"+effect,+wish"],[4,"Good app, lessons are logical and make sense. However, very frequently during the parts where you have to repeat the term for pronunciation, it doesn't register what im saying. No matter how many times I repeat it or how loud I am, it just doesn't register. This happens so often to the point where I dread the pronunciation portions a bit. Hope you guys can get this sorted out! :)","2022-01",31,"+listen"],[1,"Very disappointed. Decided to take advantage of the Black Friday lifetime sale. Made the mistake of downloading app first. The web page offers the lifetime deal. When I select subscribe, it opens the app, and there is no option for lifetime subscription. Probably a good thing as I am doubting this is a good app for me. I want to be conversational in the language. I am not trying to get a job there. Lessons about job/esumes are useless. App for business language rather than common learners.","2025-11",30,"pay,bug,wrong"],[2,"Navigation in the app is terribly confusing. Lessons are organized by Topics or Courses, but the lessons seem to overlap, and the organization is awful. I tried keeping an outside list of topics I wanted to revisit, but with inconsistent labeling of units, lessons, and parts of lessons, I'm just lost. I like the way it teaches the reasoning behind the grammar, but if I can't find my way back to the lessons, the app is infuriating.","2025-07",28,"ui"],[1,"I can no longer access any lessons without being forced to accept permissions to \"record, store, and use my voice\" for \"AI-powered features\". Declining kicks you back to the menu, despite the fact I only use Babbel for reading and writing. I can't use the program I paid for without accepting. If this is a mistake, please fix it. If this is intended, I'll be canceling.","2026-03",27,"wrong,lock,wish"],[4,"As with many other reviews, the voice recognition fails to work more than 80% of the time. Even something as simple as a vowel or 'el' are marked wrong. All permissions are allowed and microphone and wifi works great on other apps so I really hope this issue gets fixed. It can be really discouraging to see so many wrong answers even when spoken fluently.","2024-11",27,"+short,+review"],[4,"Cons: the voice recorder doesn't always catch your pronunciation maybe a good 70% of the time so not terrible. Also the weekly goal you can set is very limited i hit my \"weekly\" goal in two days (30mins each day). Also i personally wish there was more repetition but that's me. Pros: it teaches you why things are the way they are as well as howbto not only say things but spell something's as well. By no means do I find it boring i actually look forward to opening the app and putting in time.","2021-05",27,"+review,+listen,+wish"],[5,"This is the best app to use of you want to learn a new language. It doesn't do vocabulary or anything like that. The app teaches you the first steps of the language then the greetings and so on. You can also review what you learned in case you forget. I do about 3 lessons a day and I learned like 13 new words. It's awesome and I think everybody will love it!","2020-05",27,"+effect,+review"],[1,"The app is basically unusable unless you pay for a subscription. It sucks because there's a lot of good info to learn in the lessons, but you've gotta give us at least something to chew on in the free version. I'd even put up with ads for a bit more content. I'll come back if it's made a bit more accessible. There also needs some fine tuning in the 'speaking' area of daily practices. No matter how many times I say the phrase correctly, it doesn't pick it up and deems it incorrect.","2024-07",26,"pay,ad,wrong"],[1,"I wish I never signed up for this. They don't give refunds for a cancelation, I have to continue paying for the next few months of a subscription even though I never use it. The little I did use for French was a terrible experience. It continuously says the pronunciation is wrong even when pronounced correctly, terrible software. Also a scam business since it won't refund.","2023-10",26,"pay,bug,voice,wish"],[2,"It was hard to figure out how to do 1 trial lesson without paying, like 3 paywall popped up. That lesson wasn't really the right level for me so I'd like to try a harder one or two before paying but I'm blocked. Might be a good app but I'm not paying $80 to find out. This isn't a free app with \"in app purchases\", it's a paid subscription app.","2023-10",26,"pay"],[3,"App is focused on spelling, and I want to focus on conversational. Fortunately, it now forgives my small typos. Once the app thinks you mispronounced something, it has a bias towards saying you still mispronounce it. Even if you record the app saying the word and play it back. The app is very focused on getting you to use their teachers. I don't want to sit in a group learning session. (Thanks. Little dot floats all over the range. When talking, it's pegged to the right. ???)","2024-08",26,"wrong"],[5,"I enjoy every part of the ui and ability to pick up learning quickly. I give 5 stars regardless that I have a slight issue. I have been wanting to learn more than one language at a time and before I had to by in to each language. My issue is that I just re subbed like 2 months before and the new discount is twice as cheap and I was just trying to add the option to buy into the multi language without paying another 100+ right after I already paid for my sub before. I would love to hear from yall.","2024-08",26,"+short,+fun"],[5,"Not bad to keep up with language skills. I don't use the speech recognition parts of the app because I've had just so many bad experiences with ALL language learning apps regarding that and just don't want to waste time on something that won't work anyways. But generally, good coverage of topics and continued practice is helping my learning process","2022-10",26,""],[5,"It's great to learn! Amazing customer support, after posting my review they reached out to send an email showing they care about their application and getting it to work as fluid as possible. If you are having trouble with the speech recognition check the settings options to turn up or down microphone sensitivity. Mine was defaulted to high, resulting in frustrating errors during lessons. This was a easy fix thanks to their customer support!","2021-03",26,"+short,+review,+custom"],[1,"The customer service for this app is terrible. I emailed them for some help with my all access voucher 6 days ago and no response yet. The \"help\" section of the app is confusing and they make sure it's almost impossible to contact a human being (no customer service number to call). The yearly \"all access\" fee is not cheap and you can only apply it to ONE language. Not transferrable to a different language. At least I haven't found a way to do it. Not user friendly in my opinion.","2020-05",25,"ui,cs"],[1,"I really liked this app until they decided you have to consent to have your voice used for training AI or else you can't use the speaking practice feature. That and all of a sudden my app is crashing. I can't open it at all anymore. I now regret buying the lifetime subscription and wish I could refund it, because that is NOT what I paid for. If I would've known Babbel was going to pull this AI training bs I would've never bought it. Very disappointed.","2024-12",25,"pay,bug,wish"],[2,"It says that there are games as well as lessons. I have not been able to find the games. They would make practicing more fun. Also, the lessons get hard very quickly, and they don't break things down small enough to learn easily. And you have to pay money to find out if this fits your style of learning or not. l also have found that no matter what I do it doesn't recognize certain words in the voice recognition, which it then grades me on. Boo, hiss.","2025-04",25,"pay,voice"],[2,"I just went through the free trial and the app seems great in design and lesson flow. So i was just about to subscribe when it said that subscription works for only one language - and I thought that paying $83 for 12 months would give me access to the whole selection of languages, so that I can switch if I need. I wanted to get some basics in a few languages in preparation for a trip - I don't need 12 months of one. Is there an option to switch?","2019-09",25,"pay,ui"],[2,"It moves through the vocabulary way too quickly and there is absolutely no reinforcement or help when you get something wrong. Doesn't try to give you the words in more context to learn how they're used. I took Spanish in high school and did decently well. This is just a very difficult app to learn from. Definitely would not spend money on it again.","2025-12",24,"pay"],[2,"The app design feels really clumsy. Came with high recommendations and I wish I had chosen something else. You can only review a set amount of words it chooses. I wish it would let you review a set of lessons of your choosing without having to do the whole lesson over. Also, instead of one big vocabulary list- it would be nice if it sorted what you learned and grammar/pronunciation rules into groups. There's a lot of the design I find clumsy, too, but I'm out of space.","2020-10",24,"voice,ui,wish"],[5,"This is a great app to help learn a new language. I am currently learning Spanish in college but use this app as well to get ahead and broaden my vocabulary. The only thing I would suggest is to make the word blanks all the same size so that you can't guess the word based on the size of the blank. Also, there should be a setting to structure the lessons more challenging. For example, having to write in full sentences or speak a sentence without hints. Other than this, it's a great app.","2024-05",24,"+exam"],[5,"I had been using a different language learning app for years but felt like it was the same things over and over and I was losing interest. Babble offers much more variety and I feel like it helps more conversationally. I don't need more vocab, I need to know how to put it together to make conversation. Babble is definately helping with this! Worth the money!","2021-04",24,"+effect"],[1,"I used this app for about a month and I have more bad to say than good. The microphone wouldn't pick up my voice which made it difficult to practice pronunciation. I tried with and without headphones and on several devices. This really made it frustrating to use this app. I thought all of the lessons we're repetitive and not very useful. Wouldn't recommend for someone trying to become fluent in another language.","2021-02",23,"voice,repeat"],[2,"This is a great way to learn or practice a new language if you respond well to classroom-like activities. I have gotten frustrated with the app having issues recognizing my streak and making me lose progress in my lessons when I have been using it daily. I've sent messages to CS, but have been told \"we're aware of the issue\" with no changes for months. It has been hard to stay motivated and keep coming back when all that I have left is general vocab words, and there is no \"fun\" element anymore.","2025-09",23,""],[2,"I wish I'd know, from the app store that this was a totally paid experience. I wanted to see if it was better than others I tried or if my learning would progress more quickly and fully. But before I could see if it was useful or if I wanted to subscribe, I had answered a zillion questions and was hit with an \"Okay agree to pay and then you can see if you want it.\" And it's expensive.","2025-08",23,"pay,wish"],[2,"Decent app for the start of language, but in my experience there are some lessons that ask way too much for someone learning the language as you progress. I went from basic conversations to suddenly having to know the spelling of words I had seen maybe once or knowing a new case and how to conjugate it. Also some of the exercises where you are asked to spell multiple words in one blank will always be wrong even if the words are spelled correctly.","2025-10",23,""],[3,"I really like that Babbel teaches the grammar behind the language instead of just giving phrases to try and memorize. I love that I can also work on speaking, listening, reading, and writing, and the AI conversations are great practice (can't wait for more challenging levels!). But one thing that is really needed is to tell me HOW to say the word, and perhaps indicate what word(s) in a sentence I didn't pronounce correctly. It's super frustrating to get marked wrong for speaking and not know WHY","2025-01",23,"+effect,+listen"],[4,"I mostly love Babbel. I love the teaching methods, but also that there's options to review in many different ways- speaking, writing, AND flash cards. I like that they do have grammar lessons, though you may have to go looking for them. It's not always obvious where to access it unless you really explore the app. One thing I so get annoyed about is that it sometimes will use a \"streak freeze\" when I've actually completed a lesson. That can be a little frustrating. But overall I really like it.","2025-12",23,"+review,+fun,+habit"],[5,"I really liked babbel to begin with. I found the lessons to be helpful and there is no shortage of them either. I had realized I was paying for two subscriptions at once and messaged them asking if it was necessary. They said no and offered to add time to my main one to cover the difference. I think that's good customer service and not something a lot of app developers would do either. Props to them.","2018-10",23,"+effect,+short,+custom"],[5,"It's alotta funn. I've used other apps but they couldn't keep my attention. I enjoy this one . It's NOT boring and it's challenging!, Along with alotta fun! FACTS! That being said....I am sorely disappointed that it requires a credit card,which that's ok, the part that annoy'd me is.... Requiring a payment for a year in advance!!!! Sad. My loss.","2020-01",23,"+fun"],[1,"I learned nothing in 3 weeks of using this. I paid for 3 months of usage, and I haven't picked up more than 2 phrases. I picked up more with duolingo. This moves way too fast (and I was doing the review and one lesson per day), and it doesn't teach you anything useful. The pronunciations are ALL different depending on the speaker, so which one is correct? I have requested a refund and am just going to get in person classes and use Duolingo (which is FREE) instead. Waste of time and money.","2020-01",22,"pay,voice"],[1,"horrible app and zero support. After paying $100 for the use of the app, it often won't load the lessons. Sometimes, clearing the app cache will help, but mostly, I have to uninstall and reinstall the app. Tech support is worthless. I will not be renewing the subscription due to the constant technical issues. I have it installed on my phone and my tablet, and they both have their issues, so I know it is not a device issue. For the price, they should at least have a reliable app.","2025-09",22,"pay,bug"],[3,"Good for reading and writing, speaking is horrible. The talking parts always fails. I even recorded the example speech and replayed it to the mic and it still fails. If it at least replays my audio or highlight which part of the word fails, that would help so much. I wish the talking quizzes actually worked or tell me why it fails. At least in Duolingo, the speaking part passes most of the time. There seems to be a bug in the app for the talking part.","2026-06",22,"bug,voice,wish,+listen,+exam,+wish"],[4,"Has been great so far. Only issue is with the microphone/voice recognition. Sometimes works great, but on several of them, its literally impossible for me to get right. I can't type it right because it doesn't put a dash on the Babbel keyboard and when I say it, it refuses to recognize what I say correctly, after no less than 15 attempts. So there's some questions I just can't ever get right. But for the most part, seems like I could get a large amount if this language down quickly","2018-11",22,"+short"],[5,"So far, so good. I like the Beta option of having a verbal conversation; less intimidating than speaking with a real Spanish speaker as I struggle to recall words and sentence structure. This is good practice and builds confidence. I would appreciate a dictionary option. When trying to formulate my own sentences, I sometimes forget words from a lesson, but there's no way to quickly look them up.","2026-04",22,"+short,+review"],[1,"Found out about babbel through a pandora ad. The ad said chose one language for free, and then if I wanted to learn another pay for a subscription. I downloaded, and tried the app having a little fun learning not only to speak but read and write a new language. However when I tried to progress to the second \"lesson\", the app stopped me and would not let me proceed without buying a subscription first. The app seems to be a good tool, but false advertising for the app was at its best.","2020-04",21,"pay,ad"],[1,"I bought 3 months access to the French courses, it costed around 35 dollars. Upon trying to actually use my course, the app won't load, it sits there in perpetuity on a loading screen. I messaged customer support and apparently this is a known issue. If it's a known issue then why was i sold a faulty and defunct product for full price? Customer support did not offer a refund and gave me a week onto my time with the course. I wouldn't recommend this app, duolingo is more reliable.","2023-09",21,"pay,bug,cs"],[1,"Just bad. Stuck with it because I paid for lifetime access so I'd commit. Had someone who speaks German verify that some grammar is wrong and that I was pronouncing words correctly but it doesn't pick it up and just fails you over and over again where for other places you can say something barely resembling correct pronunciation and it works. Mark and avoid this app. Edit: more terrible voice recognition and not tracking streaks repeatedly and after talking to support, I've taken off a star","2025-04",21,"bug,voice,repeat"],[2,"I have completed Duolingo German, and need more German online classes. After some research I chose Babbel. The content is good, BUT the app itself not so much, especially when compared to Duolingo. It enforces its own keyboard, which is annoying. It does not allow free translations - you just use buttons with words to form sentences (on Duolingo I always forced myself to write the whole sentences). The app cannot tell you how many points you made today or previous days...","2019-06",21,"lack,ui"],[5,"Been using the program for a few weeks and really enjoying it. The lessons have enough variety that you don't get bored with the routine. I also LOVE the extra practice which includes podcasts, videos, and culture bites-just wish there were more of them. I reviewed quite a few programs before choosing Babbel and I think I made the right choice.","2022-06",21,"+short,+review,+fun,+wish"],[3,"I'm conflicted on how to rate Babbel. I'm using Babbel to learn French. For the first several months I was very happy with the app. The lessons were excellent and did a great job of explaining verb conjugation and grammar concepts. However, once I finished the B1 level lessons, it just dropped off. There were only three B2 level units and then that was the end of it. Luckily there's other subject specific lessons I can use to keep expanding my vocabulary but it's still disappointing.","2025-08",20,""],[3,"i think i am learning. However, i wish they made it more user-friendly. it takes me at least three times going over a lesson before it begins to click for me. i dont mind repeating the lessons, but the layout makes it difficult to get to your completed lessons. i can get to the past lessons, but as i progress, the older levels become more difficult to find. Your app needs a lot more opportunities to review or just make the past lessons more accessible.","2025-10",20,"repeat,ui,wish,+review,+wish"],[4,"I love the customer service! (which was literally NON existent in ANOTHER language app). I would like if they could have a ✔️ when a section is completed. I lose my place, when there's so many options (off-shoots) to take. I'm afraid, I'm missing parts of lessons. When repeating a phrase, I want the ability to click on individual words, many times its spoken too fast for me. (I do realize that some phrases have words \"run together,\") but I need to know how pronounce an individual word.","2025-07",20,"+custom"],[5,"Best app for learning foreign languages. I tried other apps but they just didn't click with me, you know? I love how you can switch around the way you study depending in what you want to do, like typing, voice, flashcards, etc. In my opinion it is directed towards children who are able to read and older. I definitely recommend and rate a five star! ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","2019-09",20,"+review"],[5,"I would love the ability to pause during \"listen to dialogue\" playback, as well as the ability to control playback speed. if I take too long trying to remember a certain word, then that ruins the rest of the dialogue playback because now I've missed an entire sentence or more. it gets overwhelming. also, after hitting pause, the option to either continue where I left off, or start over from the beginning.","2025-07",20,"+effect"],[1,"Their commercial makes no mention of the fact that this is a pay only app. I downloaded this thinking that I could use it only to find out that it's not free. Was highly disappointed. What makes this better than Duolingo and Rosetta Stone? They both have at least some free features. I'm not saying make everything free but you can at least offer something for people too poor to have credit cards... Even if it's only a couple of beginner lessons or a truly free trial where you signup with google.","2020-05",19,"pay"],[1,"it would be much more helpful if it also had the ability to read vocabulary lists, in order to learn a large number of words. although the fully intersctiv format may be effective, when tired of traveling or driving in the car, sometimes a learner just wants to be able to listen to vocabulary lists, with alternating words between the native language and foreign language.","2026-02",19,""],[5,"I wanted a language app that would be systematic and teach me the grammar rules. It also had to have Castillian Spanish. I love grammar (from studying a second language in school) so I knew I'd pick it up better with lessons, not just trying to infer. After reading lots of reviews, I decided to try Babbel and I've been very pleased. The app works smoothly and does a lot of the right things automatically (like speaking aloud). I'm not sure yet how good it's pronunciation checking is.","2026-07",19,"+review,+listen,+exam"],[5,"This is the way language needs to be taught and reinforced, explaining and putting right into practice the \"why's of the nuances\" rather than trying to memorize rules, putting conversational useful bites in place at your pace, on your phone. Instead of wasting 10-20 minutes a day on Facebook, you're speaking and comprehending quickly! Love this.","2019-02",19,"+effect,+short"],[1,"Bought the 3 months for my husband to start learning Brazilian Portuguese and it is a waste of money! Firstly the voices can't decide which brazilian accent to use, so they have multiple voice actors with different accents, I would be ok with any accent as long as it is the same, it's not consistent. Secondly the translations are wrong so I have to fix the meaning all the time. I do not recommend for Brazilian Portuguese.","2026-05",18,"pay"],[1,"I bought a 3 month subscription as the company states you could try for 20 days and be reimbursed if you didn't like it. I tried it and it's too difficult. Requested a refund the same day be emailing Customer Support as directed. Have not heard back from them. Canceled subscription online only to be informed that I still have to pay for the 3 months subscription. This is NOT the promise on the website or radio ads that I have heard. Hope this is rectified very soon.","2020-10",18,"pay,ad,cs"],[2,"Unfortunate that they don't advertise that it isn't free. It looked nice, I did the first lesson of German (A2, Unit 1 Lesson 1) and it actually explained what I was learning rather than just memorizing it without truly understanding. Sadly, I quickly realized that there was no way to do any other lessons without paying, and I'm a student and can't afford any subscriptions at the moment. Wish that would've been said at the start before I got my hopes up","2026-07",18,"pay,ad,wish"],[2,"I like the different features of this app, like how you can simulate a conversation to get more comfortable, but sometimes the sentences you learn are really awkward and will never come in handy. The pace of the lessons is also too fast. They teach you too much new information without context. I think I still prefer Duolingo, which teaches you new content gradually and simply.","2026-05",18,""],[2,"I like that the app actually teaches grammar (which that other language app leaves you to figure out on your own), but there are a number of things that make learning not enjoyable. First and foremost, the speech recognition is very bad, especially if there is any background noise whatsoever. You also don't get any guidance on what words were recognized or which weren't. And some phrases you have to say are a handful of words long. Some of the lessons are 4x the length of others.","2025-09",18,"voice"],[5,"Such a fun language learning app! The lessons cover plenty of real world situations and you definitely get a feel for how to pronounce words like a native speaker. It's also a great way to discover new cuisine. In the German lessons, I came across Schweinebraten (a roast pork dish) and found an excellent recipe online. Highly recommended for anyone looking for an enriching experience picking up a new language.","2022-11",18,"+fun"],[1,"Signed up for a three month program. I paid for it but didn't have enough time. I read and read there terms. No where did I find where I signed up for an every three month auto renewal. I missed the first auto charge... My fault. The next one I caught and cancelled. Haven't even opened the app in over 7 months. Can not get babble to contact me about it. My mistake I guess. Make sure you stay on top of them if you do stop using it. You are automatically sign up for auto payments.","2020-11",17,"wrong,cs"],[2,"The content is great, better than some alternatives. The app however seems to have a bug, about half of the time after they \"Hej\" intro it gets stuck on a white screen; then I have to force close it and try again. Also, while I can download lessons, they don't play offline. Support only tells me to reinstall the app, which does not help.","2025-12",17,"bug"],[1,"Signed up for a 3 month subscription to see if I liked the app and wanted to proceed. It didn't end up working for me which is fine. But they continued to charge my account for the next year while cutting email communication with me so I was unknowingly being charged every 3 months. Now they refuse to refund any of the payments over the last year, not even the one I caught that posted 2 days ago. Zero stars based on customer service","2024-03",16,"pay,data,cs"],[5,"I love all the different activity options ! They makes learning fun ! I am having a problem with the Podcast section of the app. I absolutely love listening to the podcasts because they are really helping me progress. I noticed that the app is not marking podcasts as complete when I finish them. I don't mind keeping track, but I wanted to report this little bug.","2026-06",16,"+fun,+listen"],[1,"Doesn't deliver as promised. Using this app I feel like I'm back in a classroom with the teacher speaking and the students listening. I thought I would be speaking more right from the beginning but I was doing more typing than speaking. But I was learning vocabulary not sentences. After you hear the words you get to type in the word in a\"fill in the blank\" sentence. Note I said a word. Like I, you, me, he, she, etc. This app is not for me.","2020-04",15,""],[1,"Before paying for anything, I wanted to see how it works. The intro was fine. When it asked me to register, I selected the email option. All it did was tell me something went wrong. I do not use social media accounts to register. Since the app basically stalls right out of the gate, I'm uninstalling. After hearing so much about it on my favorite streaming station, this is disappointing.","2019-01",14,"pay,data"],[2,"I wanted to give this 5 stars because the AI conversations are an awesome idea, but the thing that kills it for me is the voice recognition is terrible! Everytime I have an exercise that requires me to speak it never recognizes what I'm saying. I am definitely saying it correctly. The problem is it can't deal with even the slightest amount of background noise. In a quiet room it's ok, but if someone is talking or I'm walking outside it can't handle it. Fix this problem and this is 5 stars easy.","2025-07",14,"voice"],[3,"The information is okay, but the app itself isn't very user friendly. You're supposed to do a lesson and a review each day, which is fine if you can find the review. It seems you have to switch around to different tabs too much to search for what you're supposed to do. I'd rather it be that the lesson is simply followed by the next review, followed by the next lesson...etc. Also, I have the unlimited lifetime membership and yet the learning games are \"locked\".","2022-06",14,"lack,+review,+fun"],[4,"I like that the sub-lessons are broken into different units, but the speech portions can get a little tricky. In some languages, you can speak and it'll register with no problems. In other languages, it has a hard time accepting what you say even if you've said it correctly. Has a lag issue as well when waiting for it to accept your speech when you recite their words/phrases. Also when sentences are said to you, the speaker goes faster than lesson levels speed should be at","2025-06",14,""],[4,"After using Duolingo I switched to Babbel and I like it more! Feels like I'm learning things I can use in everyday conversation. However, I took one star off because of the keyboard. As with other users, I didn't know you had to hold down the keys in order to gain access to accent marks and variations on letters which left me getting things wrong even when I knew how to spell them. An introduction to the keyboard (or popup bubble) would have been helpful to avoid this.","2022-04",14,"+effect,+listen"],[4,"I bought this app to help me learn Norwegian, and I do find it to be good value for the money (especially on their black friday lifetime access sale) but the one thing that really annoys me is when the app will introduce a new word to you verbally, then expect you to know how to spell it on the following screen with zero help. I wish this would be changed. Also, at the end of every lesson there is a typing portion, and while it has hints, its annoying to he required to type.","2026-01",14,"+wish"],[5,"I just recently decided to become trilingual, I already had experience with German so I decided to try Russian and let me say it has been great. It's an easy laid back way of learning and it even comes with mini quiz like lessons and review. This app even let's you set reminders when you want to be learning. Lessons are super fast and easy and it actually helps with the learning process of a language. Highly reccomend this product to anyone trying to learn new, or brush up the old languages.","2019-09",14,"+effect,+short,+review,+lockp"],[1,"The app itself is great, but it's frankly awful to me that your \"deals\" aren't open to existing customers. You sent me at least 3 Black Friday notifications, and even though I already have a subscription and would have liked to get another one, it was only available at full price. When my subscription runs out, I will not be renewing it. Maybe I will be back next Black Friday. Maybe I will use one of the myriad of replacement apps available to me","2018-11",13,"pay,lock"],[2,"started off promising but got frustrating pretty quickly. the app refuses to let you do much review, so if you have a decent amount of time to dedicate each day, the only real option you have is to continue with the lessons, so you end up in lessons you're not really ready for. they mostly want you to be able to remember whole phrases and some of them are unnecessarily long and totally irrelevant. I had to start using other apps to reinforce my learning. might stop this one entirely soon.","2026-03",13,""],[4,"So far, I like it better than Duolingo. However, I came here to complain that the app says I made a typo every time that I use the French keyboard's accent key, instead of choosing the accented letter by holding the letter key. Also, there is no place for me to report these kinds of issues except for reviews. Otherwise, I am enjoying it quite a bit","2025-06",13,"+review,+fun,+listen"],[4,"It has good lessons. It has problems with keeping track and letting you seamlessly change between grammar and topic lessons. It requires a strong internet signal to use. Cell service sometimes works, but often doesn't when the signal isn't strong enough. I guess downloading all the images is too much. It has BIG problems with its \"streak\" functionality. The \"2 freezes per week\" is good. If you do the lesson on cell signal or late at night it will often not record that you did one.","2025-12",13,"+fun,+habit"],[5,"Best virtual learning app on the market...Period! I have tried many, as well as going the hard copy book route to learn. I now use them all in combination but Babbel is hands down the major reason I am learning the languages quickly. They keep adding more stuff into the app as well. This is a must have for anyone trying to leanr a new language that has a busy lifestyle. you can just literally squeeze a lesson in on the go, or during downtime. EXCELLENT JOB WITH THIS APP!","2019-05",13,"+short"],[2,"I made the assumption that this would let me learn one free lesson a day, and I would have to pay the $100 to get more than that. I was incorrect. It gives you exactly one free lesson. This is an app that lets you download it for free and gives you exactly one taste of their (admittedly excellent) teaching strategy, then demands $100+ for even one more lesson.","2026-08",12,"pay,wrong"],[3,"I like the variety of ways to learn and practice any chosen language, but the biggest thing holding it back is the speech recognition. People have been pointing it out for years, and it is still giving users trouble even when everything is up to date. Please fix your speech recognition instead of just telling people to update or reinstall the app.","2026-04",12,"voice,wish"],[4,"While I enjoyed the app thoroughly, I found that I was being billed twice: Once for $119.88 and then again, in the same month for $77.94. They have the same serial number. I have just cancelled my subscription (after unsubscribing to the auto-pay), but I fear I may still get billed, since the double billing did not appear to be aware of duplication, or additional fees.","2024-02",12,"+fun"],[4,"I like Babbel, but the app has started to have errors lately, such as marking correct answers that require you to type more than one word into a prompt incorrect. I wish error reporting was easier. I also wish I could pin specific parts of lessons. Sometimes a grammar concept is introduced in the middle of a lesson and I can never seem to find it again.","2025-10",12,"+wish"],[5,"So far it has been great! I love how it gives you reviews of everything and has pronunciation for everything as well as pictures. I also love how it has you spell the words and tests you multiple times with each new word. I feel like the spelling helps me to recognize the word visually and pay more attention. I enjoy seeing the words used in sentences and trying to figure out the meaning before I looking. it helps me see which words change form when used in a sentence and I learn more words.","2019-05",12,"+effect,+review,+fun,+listen,+exam"],[1,"After 3 questions, it put me as a high level beginner. Seems like they just want to make money making you spend more time on the app. Another person I know that is fluent in both languages was also set to beginner. That's scammy and a rip off. We shared levels after the placement test and decided not to spend money after catching the rip off scam. Save your money.","2025-11",11,"pay"],[1,"I paid for the subscription and it doesn't even work. Keeps taking me to the wrong language and tries to make me pay again. Worst part, I did a yearly subscription so basically just wasted a hundred dollars. I'm sure the language learning is great but that doesn't matter if you can't access it and since you have to pay first to figure that out I would definitely recommend NOT getting an extended subscription. In addition to that the only lesson it actually allowed to take was how to say hi/bye","2024-01",11,"pay"],[1,"This app goes way too quickly for me unfortunately. Long conversations and phrases are required, instead of the basics of pronouns and conjunctions. I stuck with it for 3 weeks, but only got frustrated since I don't know the content that I am being tested on. Also, there is a pronunciation portion that is very frustrating. After pronouncing the phrase precisely, the app says, that's ok you'll get it, even though I said it correctly. Not worth the expensive fee for the app.","2020-08",11,"pay,bug,voice"],[1,"1. they don't tell you that once you purchase to learn a language that you cannot leave that language and use the amount of time you purchased on a different language. You have to pay for each language separately. 2. The app doesn't help me learn a new language the way I would be able to obsorb the information. 3. App doesn't always recognize when you repeat a word back correctly. Overall find it frustrating and a waste of money/time.","2022-01",11,"pay,repeat"],[5,"Spanish learner here, I like it. the app provides detailed explanations of grammar and pronunciation. it explains how other parts of a country or region say things. I'm learning the Latin American version of Spanish. it's been pretty helpful so far I just wish it didn't stop at the B1 level curriculum. and because it already has the original Spain region. I would have to start all the way over on the Spain version to continue the course. I bought the lifetime subscription. definitely worth it","2026-08",11,"+effect,+listen,+wish"],[5,"Babble is a great app for learning a new language. I literally just downloaded the app about 10 minutes ago and I already understand three phrases perfectly. It starts out free I don't know if they ask you to pay later on but if they do I will because it seems well worth it. I want to travel I want to explore the world and learn languages effectively and efficiently and I think that this app is perfect for that.","2020-03",11,"+effect,+short,+free"],[5,"I used duolingo before and felt like i was running on a treadmill a bit. I like how this is more conversational. It feels like I'm gaining understanding a bit faster. One thing I would like babbel to adopt is an option to have more notifications/reminders to practice if you haven't. Also, notifications telling you how you are doing in relation to your goal.","2023-02",11,"+lockp"],[1,"I wanted to try this. The trial requires a credit card and I want to try it first!! it does lure you into giving up your email and sign up BEOFRE spring that their is no really FREE trial. If someone truly likes it they will pony up the money. You lost a customer before you even had me. I just wanted to try a week without commitment!","2026-05",10,"pay"],[1,"I feel like if you're new to a language you shouldnt start with verb conjugations. Im not a stupid person, but this app has succeeded in making me feel pretty damned stupid. You shouldn't be buried within the first 5 lessons. Not to mention that I bought a years subscription and found out the hard way that I can't choose a different language without purchasing another subscription.","2020-01",10,"pay"],[1,"Only suitable for beginners. Very simple lessons. If you already have a solid foundation in a language that you would like to improve on, Babbel will not take you to the next level. Another nuisance is that the streak freezes don't work. If you miss a day and still have streak freezes left, they won't get applied automatically, i.e., you'll be starting from day one the next day. This app also constantly resets the streak to zero, even if you practice daily and don't use any streak freezes!","2025-12",10,"bug,data,wish"],[1,"DON'T BUY THIS!! I got the best subscription, 1 time payment lifetime access all the languages available. 3 days later I'm still trying to get someone to help me because I have 0 access to the material I purchased. They sent an invoice and money was taken from my bank account. They claim no payment received. When you message customer support, they don't message back and forth till its resolved. They give you generic responses and you're talking to a new person every time. They won't help.","2024-05",10,"pay,bug,data,cs"],[2,"Really disappointing. Something seriously wrong with this app. No matter how loud and clear I pronounced 'si' the most simple word in Spanish, it still rejects my answer. Really doesn't help me when I know 100 percent that I'm stating the word properly, but it still rejects my answer, not good forconfiden.Also something about the format that is boring to the point where I just want to do something else. Seems like y'all would come up with more fun ways to learn, so that it would be more engaging","2022-05",10,"repeat"],[5,"Enjoying the app and the techniques it uses. Will update after I have progressed further. After further use, it is a great app for learning a new language. It isn't just a mimic to learn how to say words. It goes through the whole class learning process of nouns, subjects masculine and feminine, along with sentence structure and much more. Very through.","2023-01",10,"+fun,+exam"],[1,"I rate this app a zero. The verbage was crazy I thought it was going to be $7.50 a month not $89 right off the bat and then when you cancel they keep your money anyway. I will not be able to pay my rent because of this. They should make it clearer and once you get that shock you should be able to cancel right away I use the app for less than 8 hours","2023-02",9,"pay"],[1,"I wouldn't use it because it's not motivating me to do it everyday. The app is pretty boring. I would like to type the words not unscramble them. When you start it doesn't start off with the basics of learning different languages. It's pretty bland. Personally Duolingo helps me get motivated to do it everyday and the app is pretty fun and it let's me type the words in the language that I choose to do and no bland and the microphone works great.","2020-07",9,"voice,repeat"],[3,"3 of 5 for a big reason - it's expensive, and the listening part of the model is so clearly broken that I can't tell if I'm actually pronouncing things right or not. It chooses to break for entire sections of a lesson at a time. For the money spent, that's a little lame. will be continuing to do my best to get my money's worth and hope for future updates. other than that it's awesome, way better than the dumb green bird competition, but this one issue is a major L for me.","2026-04",9,"pay,bug,+fun,+listen"],[5,"Intuitive and easy to use. I love that you learn complete phrases and or sentences as opposed to single words. The format and repetition of material is excellent. I'm trying to brush up on my Spanish as I teach English as a Second Language and have many Spanish speaking students. I would recommend that my students try the English language version of this app if it is free/affordable as I'm impressed with the format of lessons.","2018-09",9,"+short,+review,+free"],[5,"Я loving learning русский! With babble its made it easy. Not only am I learning to speak it, but also read and write it! Just a single course a day will make a big impact. I try and use what I've learned in real life, which makes a huge difference! Its enjoyable and easy! They really get into detail and repetitive, but different with what you are being taught. Way better than high school class! Lol.","2020-11",9,"+effect,+short,+fun,+exam"],[5,"just started, but I really like it right off the bat. I registered an account first, then searched for the discount, which was easy,and snagged lifetime for $239. It instantly linked to my account, and I was off and learning after an assessment, of course. It was seamless and exceptionally smooth. I was engaged in the process within seconds of making the purchase. The level of lesson felt spot on for me. I am very optimistic about my learning experience!!","2025-10",9,"+short"],[1,"I used the free 7 days trial and cancelled it within two days. Despite that, I was still charged 100$ for a yearly subscription. By the time I realised I was charged despite canceling, the 20 days period was over and I wasn't eligible for a refund. This is a predatorial behaviour. I would not recommend this app, particularly considering the more popular, free to use alternatives who do not rely on stealing money from their customers.","2023-06",8,"pay"],[1,"I was going to try this app after seeing commercials on it... but it doesn't even have certain Asian languages like Japanese, Korean, and Chinese... which is a bit infuriating since I have been looking all over the place for an app to learn Japanese where ir has speaking exercises... honestly if you could add one of those languages I'll be willing to give it a shot otherwise no","2024-07",8,""],[1,"Went to choose the language I wanted to learn and babble doesn't even offer it. Japanese is a fairly common and robust language. One of the oldest, and they don't show it in the list. Major F-up on babbles part. Didn't even get past 2 taps in the app before I'm deleting. Have a far larger list than 8 languages to learn before you advertise as one of the best apps to learn from. Honestly, a joke sell out that pays for more advertisement than it says from what I can see.","2022-02",8,"ad"],[1,"Might actually be a better language learning system that some of its better looking free competitors. The price is high for a product with an unrefined visual style, but I mostly looked past that. What I can't stand is that they charge your auto-renewal without even an emailed invoice a few days in advance. It's tacky and seems to be the only way most people would sign up for a 2nd year.","2019-02",8,"pay"],[1,"Voice recording (e.g. the speaking portion of the courses), suddenly has stopped working. It either lags and times out after you speak, or doesn't recognize what you are saying at all. The courses can't be completed without passing the speaking portion, so the app has become a waste of money.","2021-08",8,"pay,bug"],[1,"Not only is it way too cocky in ads and claims it can teach someone another language in 3 weeks, but it also has such a small amount of language options! It doesn't even have chinese and Japanese and other asian and non-english-alphabet-using languages. Japanese, the language I've been learning for the past 2 years, is on almost every language app, including the best and original one, which I suggest, Duolingo. I don't see how the most cocky and confident one has literally 5 languages on it.","2019-09",8,"ad"],[2,"Well... the first lesson was great. And helpful... and fun as well. But do I only get one lesson free and then have to pay for ALL of the others? Because if that's the case I'm just deleting the app. I can't afford it. I'm so sick of apps being great and then out of nowhere they hit you with \"monthly payments\". Nothing can ever just be free anymore. So if I have to pay for all the other courses I'm just deleting the app cause it'd just be wasting space on my phone.","2019-11",8,"pay"],[2,"Beginner levels one and two are great but it goes downhill from there. My biggest complaint is the review system. Its more like memorizing entire phrases rather than the meaning of individual words, making it hard to form your own sentences in convo. There's no way to review the grammar rules without taking the lessons over again, which are quite long. I find myself using Duolingo more often and learn more from the repition, different combinations of words, and easy to reference grammar rules.","2019-01",8,""],[3,"The app does teach structured lessons fundamentally from a personalized starting point but then doesnt quite explain the why. The free learning is pretty much non-existent and jumps to 3 month subscription minimal. Which the price is expensive for an app. To me it seems pretty high for the flat learning style. Theres nothing really competitive that drives you like contests, freebies to be won, or anything that puts a spin on the learning aspect. For that price I want the app to clutch me in.","2026-08",8,"pay,+fun,+free"],[4,"I love it so far, I just think it auto- progresses through the pages where it says 'study the sentences' with picture and phrase--too quickly. That should be user controlled. I'll check if there's a setting to do that but if not, there should be! otherwise I love how it veries my answer as I select it without having to click the answer, then another check my answer button and wait for a dumb little owl to dance around and throw confetti at me.","2026-04",8,"+short"],[5,"This is a pretty good app. It does help you learn correct pronunciation on words in different languages, and gives you test and makes you repeat words several different ways so they will 'Stick' in your memory. However $14.95 a month is a bit much for an app I don't use often anymore.","2022-11",8,"+listen,+exam"],[1,"Lesson one is just the start and you expect me to pay the minimum of 26$ a month just to go on to the NEXT LESSON +more!? That's just a knock off. What I'm trying to say is, let people do more lessons before you go knock off with a subscription. That'll get people more hooked. I would've spent my money if you just would've let me experience more about learning the language and learning about the app. It's sas really. I was expecting to atleast get a few lessons in, but was restricted into one.","2020-06",7,"pay"],[1,"👎👎👎PLEASE READ BEFOR YOU DOWNLOAD THE APP !!!! Useless. I wanted my wife to learn some Spanish too be able to communicate with my patterns, I downloaded the app and you have to pay before you can even try it. Also to expensive!! that's why they advertised it too much on the radio and youtube. They know smart people aren't paying for it. Try Duolingual is FREE. I'll update this review every other day so it remains on the top.","2021-01",7,"pay,ad"],[2,"Mediocre at best. Simple and easy to use, but most of the lessons involve nothing more than repeating sentence fragments with no context. I've learned some German vocabulary, but I feel as if my grasp of grammar is actually a bit weaker than before I started using this thing, mainly due to lack of practice and overemphasis on rote repetition of basic phrases.","2019-05",7,"repeat"],[3,"Installed to try it out & see it's teaching method. The initial experience is okay; just know you don't HAVE to purchase a subscription to try out one very short lesson. Just hit \"back\". I would be nice if the app didn't intentionally obfuscate this option. The demo is too short. It doesn't give you nearly enough information to commit to their subscription rates. Finally, a language I'd like to learn is missing—Japanese. I'm surprised they don't offer Korean or Chinese, either.","2023-08",7,"pay,wish,+short,+wish"],[4,"So far, I think babbel is pretty good. I haven't picked up Spanish since high school, so it's a nice refresher for the lessons I already learned. I'm giving the app four stars bc of lack of games. There were three games when I started, but they had since removed the game with the cat on a boat. (I'm not sure why). I will raise my review to 5 stars when they add several other games for practice that add a variety to the ones they already provide. 😸","2024-07",7,"+effect,+review,+fun,+exam"],[5,"I'm liking Babbel a lot more than Duolingo (which kinda went off the rails and lost its way). Straightforward with minimal distracting gamification. There are actually meta educational components about the language - grammar rules, exceptions. I do wish it got into more details about pronunciation - especially with French as the rules (or lack thereof) make it complicated. Ideally it could even correct my pronunciation someday. The lifetime license is also a pretty decent deal.","2026-08",7,"+listen,+wish"],[5,"I like that there are several ways to practice and learn and there's no games and annoying rewards and leagues. Just learning! I like to practice what I've learned before learning more and sometimes it cuts me off from practice and I must do another lesson, but it's really a great app! Really like the hands free audio options too!","2026-05",7,"+effect,+fun,+listen,+free"],[5,"so far the free lessons seem to be very easy as I am just starting out but I have had Spanish courses in the past. the lessons are very simple and straightforward and seem to be well constructed as teaching tools . there is also a wide variety of options as far as what kind of courses you want to take and you can go back and forth between them learning how words fit together and the audio pronunciation helps enforce learning by hearing how they should be spoken how they sound .✓amt.b4 $ pay","2022-07",7,"+effect,+short,+listen,+free"],[5,"I have had this app for several months now and I continue to find it impressive in useful. There are so many lessons in each one of the levels and the way they approach to learning is super useful. For example not only do you read and write but you also listen at the same time. I have some language experience from my college Years but it has been a long time. I think that the subscription fee is well worth it as it allows you to start and stop whenever you want. I love this app!","2021-07",7,"+exam"],[5,"I have used a few dozen Spanish apps, this is the most comprehensive by a mile. The \"Auido Recaps\" are as good, or better, than Pimsleur, and the daily lessons are as addictive as Duolingo. It actually explains grammar. It can sometimes be daunting, and throw one word you know in with half a dozen you don't, but it is surprisingly effective. I am still in the beginner stages, but this is my favorite of these apps. An audio-only option for commutes or walks, and great lessons.","2026-03",7,"+effect,+fun,+listen,+habit"],[1,"I just downloaded this app to try refreshing and improving my Chinese from high school and college that I haven't used the past 4ish years. The first screen I encountered to create my account wanted me to select what language I want to learn... but Chinese isn't an option. In fact, most languages aren't an option. No point in setting up a trial account if I can't choose the language I want.","2021-09",6,"data"],[1,"2 big problems. 1: I have selected Spanish (Latin American), and it's still trying to use the European version. The pronunciationtion is completely wrong. And 2, half of the free modules don't even work. I'm getting errors all over the place. And I'm definitely not going to be spending money if I don't even know if the app is any good.","2024-09",6,"pay,bug,voice"],[2,"The app is pretty good so far, little overwhelming with it's layout, but it works. My one MASSIVE issue. Subscriptions. This unfortunately has to stop. Not everyone has the ability to pay for subscription after subscription, and the fact it's the first thing you see if very soulless and corporate slop. UPDATE: No its worse. The fact you only have access to ONE lesson before being forced to pay is disgusting.","2026-08",6,"pay,ui"],[3,"It was advertised as a free app, it said 'sign up to start learning for free' but after you finish the beginners lesson you discover you have to pay to continue. If youre gonna make it cost money *state it in your ads*. Dont advertise it as free. Other than that, from the little I saw, it looked nice. Unfortunately I dont have the money to pay for monthly subscriptions to learn a new language. Especially since Duolingo is completely free...","2019-11",6,"pay,ad,+free"],[5,"I received some errors in spelling until I figured out that you must also include the blank spaces provided in addition to the letters as you choose them to spell the words in the exercise. A learning curve I suppose. Also if the app is installed on a phone with a smaller 5.5 inch screen as I have. Some of the answers will appear below and out of sight. Be sure to scroll upward if you don't see the immediate answer. Great app. Well reinforced learning...","2019-10",6,""],[5,"its a great app, absolutely outstanding work. I would GREATLY recommend to anyone wanting to learn almost any language. Definately something I will be using, but not exactly what I was looking for. I'm looking for an app that can teach me Old Norse. If you could add that to this app then that would be great! If not, then could someone point me in the direction of an app that can teach me Old Norse? Other than that, this app is great for learning languages","2019-03",6,"+wish"],[5,"I am using Babel to pick up on my Spanish. I've always wanted to become fluent and Babel has made it easy to continue my learning by doing lessons throughout the day. The repetition through typing and speaking and matching as well as the conversational examples make it easy to learn new words and phrases. The app response to speech practice is encouraging and has helped me improve my accent. I am loving this app!","2020-03",6,"+effect,+short,+review,+listen,+exam,+wish"],[5,"I personally did not follow through with more lessons but the ones I did were awesome! I may go back to it if things around me settle down a bit. It was fun and I actually retained what I was learning. I could go at my own pace and review when and what I needed to. Customer service was great, and nice as well, when I needed to contact them to take a break in my subscription. Thank you!","2019-07",6,"+review,+fun,+custom"],[1,"I can not get this app to properly display on either my tablet or my phone. During lessons, lower part exercise is cut off, making it impossible to make any progress when using my phone. It gets worse on the tablet. I can't complete a lesson because the pages don't scroll forward . It's as if the exercise just simply gets stuck. It is not an internet issue, it is an app issue. Perhaps this is not designed for android users. I just signed up for the courses, and i'm gonna request a refund.","2025-03",5,"pay,bug,ui"],[1,"I knew I didn't like the app and knew an automatic payment would come out, so I followed the instructions I found online to keep it from renewing and charging me again. A payment of nearly 50 dollars still came out and when it did I only had an email to contact. I've been waiting and I still haven't heard anything back yet. If it's so hard to cancel properly then babbel really should either have a phone number to call or they shouldn't make you sign up under automatically renewing plans.","2020-08",5,"pay,cs"],[1,"Just another company that doesn't stand behind its product, and hides behind a horrible auto-renew subscription that doesn't even give you the courtesy of a notice that another payment is about to process. And when you get your notice that they charged you, and you want a refund, you're screwed. They have no contact info on their website, and they only let you cancel your auto-renew, so you're still stuck for a whole effing year of a service you don't use or want, and no money back. Don't use!","2023-01",5,"pay,bug,cs"],[1,"Maybe it was in the fine print or something that I didn't read, but I didn't realize you can't use the app unless you buy a subscription. That's unbelievably stupid, no way am I paying for an app that I don't even know if I like! They give you 1 lesson, 4 words, and then you're not able to do anything else until you pay for the subscription. How am I supposed to know if the app is any good if the most you give us is 4 flipping words? No thanks, I'd rather learn from YouTube or the creepy owl.","2023-05",5,"pay"],[1,"I'm very disappointed. 90% of the time, I can't get my lessons to load at all. When I can get them to open, I really don't find the lessons to be any better than free apps like DuoLingo. The speaking exercises just don't work, because no matter what I say/how I say it, it doesn't register that I'm saying it correctly. The word could be \"no\", and I could say it 50 times exactly as I'm supposed to and it still says it's wrong or just acts like I never spoke. Huge waste of money.","2022-08",5,"pay"],[3,"It would've been an excellent game for learning Spanish, but if you arent able to pay for it when it surprises you that you need to in order to continue after about two minutes in, then you shouldn't bother downloading it. If you are able, then go for it its worth it. I downloaded something very similar as far as, fun and easy to learn fast , for free called speak tribe or something. Good luck!","2020-02",5,"pay,bug,+short,+fun,+free"],[5,"Im Impressed. unlike most foreign language programs, this one puts you in situations where you have to think about what you have already seen so you try harder to remember how words are said and spelled. You have lessons and correct your mistakes then the cruches are taken away. The too easy is taken away so you try harder to remember what you have already done....if that makes sense. If all you have to do is pick multiple choice, your not going to retain what you have reviewed as well.","2019-06",5,"+effect,+short,+review"],[5,"It's great! Yes it costs some money but it's not even that much and it's so worth it, you will learn so much especially if you try not to miss any day's. If you want to learn a language go with babbel, I did duolingo for so long and I realised I couldn't even have a simple conversation in another language. But then with babbel I can kinda have a conversation in german but I only had it for 3 weeks so think of how much you will learn in just a year!","2020-03",5,"+short"],[5,"I like this app a lot so far. It has nice quick sessions, it progresses nicely, explains language rules as you go, and presents practice in a variety of forms: speaking, typing, and selecting from possible answers. The only thing I'd like to see changed is either a more obvious way to add the tilde or more than one reminder for this in early lessons. I don't recall ever seeing directions for this.","2021-04",5,"+short,+lockp"],[5,"Babbel developers, I understand 100% that course fees cover expenses to improve the app. The app runs beautifully. My only issue was that the advertisements I have seen never mentioned course fees. I've noticed that a lot of other people have had that issue as well. To prevent any further confusion you should state clearly in your commercials that some courses only offer one free lesson while other courses can have, as you stated in your response, up to 80 free lessons. Thank you for your time.","2022-08",5,"+free,+wish"],[5,"I like these lessons. took Spanish in school many years ago, but have forgotten most, particularly because I didn't have anyone to talk it with. I am enjoying this time to relearn. The amount of new words in each lesson boggles my mind at times when I am still trying to get the 'person' learned. Younger people likely pick it up more easily. Remembering the tense and spelling are the most difficult.","2020-09",5,"+effect,+fun,+exam"],[5,"it annoys me when people give this app a bad review just because it's not free. you pay for the quality. free language learning apps are nowhere near as good as this app. I've tried every single free language learning app and they've all disappointed me and I wasn't learning effectively. I'm paying $10.50 a month to get full access to all 13 languages on this app and that's a damn bargain. if you're serious about learning new languages, I highly recommend it! I tell all my viewers about it!","2019-05",5,"+effect,+review,+free"],[1,"Can't figure out which words in a sentence I mispronounce. No search for a word to practice. Can't find a list of numbers. No real help function Very disappointed in Babble. New problem. it won't continue a lesson if it doesn't understand a word. No continue past the word. Stuck on pronunciation of number seven in French. I can't possibly be that far off.","2023-02",4,"bug,voice"],[1,"This came up on a search for learning Korean, but after downloading it, I found out that Korean is not offered. (And by the way, look around guys, I think you'll find there's a lot more demand for Korean lessons these days than Dutch and Norwegian.) I think it's pretty sleazy to advertise products you don't actually sell just to keep your download rate up. Frankly if I found out tomorrow that Korean was now offered I think I'd pass just out of annoyance.","2019-11",4,"ad,bug"],[1,"Not enough review of the alphabet & sounds. Very advanced wording rather than language basics. For languages which use different alphabets (like Russian) its hard to remember the sounds each letter makes. Babel introduces the letter and sound but rarely goes back to it, they just expect you to remember. I'm using DuoLingo as well to learn Spanish, they force you to master the lesson before you can move on. Babbel moves on too quickly & introduces ridiculous phrases one would rarely use.","2021-11",4,"lack"],[1,"Obnoxious. It's hard to navigate the app, there isn't much you can do, and its even harder to get rid of. You can't just unsubscribe from emails through the emails. You have to log in and they logged me out then I had to fight with them about my password and they never sent that email. To delete you have to do it on your computer not your phone. They make it as annoying as possible to break up with them. Do not give them your info.","2023-07",4,"pay,data,ui"],[1,"Customer service sucks not really helpful at all. See anytime I say a number in Spanish it pops up in English for example i say once it pops up 11 every time and customer service claim they can't help me. Ok okay just when I was coming to grips with the numbers problem now when I speak into the thing it won't put the capitalized letter if it's the first letter so it's saying the answer is wrong. And it wants hyphens and accents but there's no option on the keyboard in the app come on you killing me now I'm paying for this thing","2018-12",4,"pay,bug,cs"],[1,"Was charged 179.98 for ONE purchase of the 50% off 89.99 every 12 months. A glitch happened in your system saying i had lost internet connection and then told me I already had the product. I still don't have access to the rest of the product and I will be seeking a full refund soon. I clicked the subscription ONCE and somehow getting two 89.99 purchases on my bank. Not cool.","2023-01",4,"pay,bug"],[2,"I'm very disappointed in this app. I thought it would grow on me, but missed the opportunity for a free refund. The voice recognition (listening to you talk) is slow, and constantly says it can't hear me (despite every other voice app on my phone behaving well). And I don't know what criteria they are using to determine the order of words to teach in the lesson, but it is NOT in order of frequency used. I very much regret buying a lifetime membership. waste of money!!!!","2026-09",4,"pay,bug,voice"],[4,"So far mostly great, except for the section where you have to press the squares with letters or parts of words to fill in the blanks-- seems it's often laggy and I find I have to press a square, wait a half second, then press the next. Maybe it's my phone, maybe it's an intentional part of the design/learning process, but I'm finding it frustrating. I also had to chuckle a bit that the section on ordering (alcoholic) drinks (one beer, please) started with a picture of a child with an ice cream","2025-02",4,""],[4,"I have learned much with this app. I am determined to get to know it better though it does have some glitches. I can't see the whole sentence a third if the time. It needs to have a smaller font ot bigger text box maybe. Sometimes it gives you the answer, which is not good practice. Also, 25% of the time when I use the speaker function it says try again no matter how perfectly I say the phrase or word. I still love the app, I just want the little things fixed for the price I have to pay.","2021-03",4,"+effect"],[5,"I love this app. I have tried other language training apps and programs and soon loss interest because they were hard to use and didn't give me practical use of the language. Babbel is engaging and I use it almost every day. Because it is on my phone if I am somewhere and have a few minutes, I just go to it. I am 67 and I am no longer discouraged about learning another language.","2020-09",4,"+short,+habit"],[5,"I chose Spanish because it is the language, I currently don't speak, that I most often hear others speaking in my area, etc. I made some mistakes, but that's part of learning & have only completed the first session. App is easy to use. I'm hopeful I will soon have Spanish as second language I can speak, understand & write! It looks promising so far!! 😁🙂","2019-09",4,"+short"],[5,"I've tried Babbel a few times before and didn't like it. I'm really serious and more dedicated to learning a language now and decided to give Babbel another chance. Paid for a six month subscription and I am not disappointed at all! It's truly amazing! I love it! And I intend on purchasing another subscription once I finish this language and move onto the next! One of my favorite language apps!","2021-04",4,""],[5,"Obviously one must pay for the subscription, which I think is a little expensive but I was lucky to get a student discount. Other than that, the app is great! A clean UI, easy navigation, easy and decently made and length lessons, and I have learned a lot with the norwegian course. Five stars for me!","2021-01",4,"+effect,+short"],[1,"I paid for full access weeks ago. I made pretty good progress. All of a sudden It ask me to login and once I did all progress was gone and they were prompting me to pay for courses. I just paid 3 weeks ago for full access for six months. I called and sent numerous emails, no response. I don’t want to give up so I just paid again.","2020-10",3,"pay,data,cs"],[1,"Nothing at all FREE! NOTHING! What a waste of my time. A total lie, they say learn free, you get about 30 seconds of free content, then you're done! Liars! Edit: responding to developer's remarks, there's nothing free besides the first 1 minute session. They keep saying up to 80 lessons free, and that is not true at all! The developer has responded again, the point is that I don't want to learn 30 seconds of 80 languages, I want to use the app for one language for several lessons before I pay.","2024-06",3,"pay"],[1,"Don't waste your time! Terrible experience. The app is pretending to be free and after 1 lesson you need to pay a lot of money. Maybe if you wouldn't spent so much money on advertisement, you could charge less. In addition the level placement is a complete joke. Instead of checking the actual knowledge the app just asks a few subjective questions and then randomly puts you some low level.","2020-02",3,"pay,ad"],[1,"All I want to do is 5 minutes per day. This is set to either 10 or 2 minutes. The explanations are rife with jargon and no easy way to learn the jargon. Just sucks the fun out this - drudgery. Furthermore, the lessons dont seem to be logically connected. You start a lesson covering dependent clauses, then it shifts to vocabulary never covered before. If you get it wrong, good luck figuring out why you're wrong. I'm going to cancel this as soon as possible. Can't stand paying for this anymor","2025-02",3,"pay"],[1,"Absolutely disgusting! I decided to pay 12.00 and some change for one month and I have 2 more charges on my bank account for 2 3 month services that I did not purchase. There is no way to contact a real person to dispute the charges. Not only did that happen but when I wrote them an email I never got a response. I then went in to the app and it will not let me progress from the trial even though I was charged 3 times. This app is bad do not use!!","2020-09",3,"pay,data,cs"],[1,"First your only allowed 2 lessons before you have to pay. You barely get to see if babbel is good. Also I can't find the area to delete my acount and help isn't working. The settings area has weird text like: Se T T In G S So it makes it impossible to read. The help often only covers Apple and pc not android. And when I found something to help with the text issue. There was no accessibility tab. So no do not reccomend and cause a bunch of problems.","2022-12",3,"pay"],[1,"This app used to be pretty good. I can not say that now. I have had issues signing in for months. It takes me 20-30 minutes to sign in each and every time. I do not have this kind of free time. I want to study a language 15-20 minutes a day. Not waste my time. Babble app does not recognize my email address when signing in. Yet sends password reset to the same email address? I have reported and requested help but not joy. Time to shop another language app.","2023-10",3,"data"],[1,"Idk how this is a name to be recognized as a language tool. They lie about what languages they offer. They spam your email and you can't unsubscribe from emails, only cancel account. When I said I speak Spanish very well (they ask for you fluency), they started me off with ”hola\"& \"gracias\". The whole planet knows what \"hola\" means. To reset your progress, you need to contact customer support who didn't get back to me or reset. This is the worst language app I've ever come across. beyond words..","2023-03",3,"pay,data,cs"],[2,"Completely counterintuitive, and confusing layout. Often it's really hard to tell what they want you to do. As well the translations can too often be contradictory and out right wrong. I will give them credit for grammar explanations though. Also there's not much in the way of personalizing your experience. Like speech speed for example. Transitions are painfully slow, and whenever you exit the app, it exits the lesson and you have to reload it.","2026-09",3,"bug,voice,ui"],[2,"I put in that I'm intermediate in Spanish (I am trying to refresh) and I am still having to go through lessons about the alphabet. Where would it have started me if I said I was a beginner? The voice recognition is bad. To get it to recognize simple words, I have to enunciate each syllable unnaturally. Overall, I think this could possibly be good for new learners but I don't think it's worth the cost for anyone further along than that. I regret the purchase.","2023-01",3,"pay,voice"],[2,"Update. I emailed over a week ago and still have no received a response. I have payed for a subscription that I have been unable to use for two weeks now. German. Was great until recently when the app won't pick up on me repeating things back. It cuts off before I'm done saying something and or sometimes doesn't cut off when I'm done. Hard to get a good score if it always says it can't understand or hear you. Please fix!","2020-10",3,"pay,bug,repeat,wish"],[3,"been having a lot of issues with connecting to babbel lately. when I log in things won't load even when I'm connected to Internet in my own home. I'm also having issues with the \"fix my mistakes feature\" it isn't working right and makes me redo the entire lesson instead of just the mistakes like it used to. been really happy with babbel up until this point. I'm at 53 days straight and that's just because I've been hounding the app until it works.","2026-05",3,"bug,data,wrong"],[4,"it's a great app. wish there would be flashcards for subject and verb conjugations and tenses. I want. he wants. I wanted, he wanted, I will want, he will want for lots of various commonly used verbs. want, pay, see, give, go, etc. I have to use Google translate and make my own. also when a sentence is given, the words in the sentence don't necessarily match the actual literal translation, so you don't really learn the words because the words don't really mean what it says.","2026-09",3,"+review,+wish"],[4,"I like that there are several different modalities of learning. Both recognition and recall are utilized. There is a good variety of vocabulary being taught. I like that verbs are conjugated. The only reason I didn't give it a five star is because certain things aren't explained that I don't understand. For instance, there are three different forms of the word \"there\" and I'm confused about when to use each one. That was never explained. in general though it is a great program and a good deal!","2018-12",3,""],[4,"Granted you have to pay for this and I haven't gotten too far but I prefer this over Duolingo. So far it has taught me phrases and stuff which is awesome but after a little time I feel like I need to be able to engage in conversations to complete training. I use this app to learn languages I don't need or will never use in the near future so it's a bit harder to flow a full conversation and learn outside the phrases babbel teaches. But at least I know please and thank you lol","2021-01",3,""],[4,"Great app. My one disappointment is that they showed monthly subscription options. I selected the 1 year. Which is $6.95 per month but then charged me the entire year at once. This is deceptive and had me want to cancel and request a refund at first. Be warned it's not a monthly subscription. They will charge you the entire subscription at one time.","2018-10",3,""],[5,"Highly upset, I paid for a year and the further I get into the lessons, I'm realizing the keyboard within the app won't let me use ('). So whenever I need to use it for the writing portion of a lesson, its beings marked incorrectly! French : \"Tu es d'où\" or Je n'habite pas... I got wrong because the keyboard did not give me the option for the ' in the sentences! UPDATE, False alarm! 😁 If you hold the comma button down it pops up other special character options. All is well again.","2020-05",3,"+short,+habit"],[5,"An app above the rest! Solid lessons, make lesson goals per learning speed then hit them. But even after that there's MORE. Live professors that help with anything you struggle with, reviews, and even memory retention games, yes I said games not just match word or flash card games. Games that ACTUALLY test your meddle and intellect with what you've already learned! I've been recommending this app to coworkers and they enjoy it!","2022-04",3,"+effect,+review,+fun,+exam"],[5,"Babble is the most comprehensive language app I have used. After one year of daily practicing German with this app, I went to work in Germany, I was able understand more German than I ever anticipated. I was still nervous to speak, but when I did I was well understood and people were shocked to learn that I had only been learning German for one year.","2018-11",3,"+habit"],[5,"Excellent selection of languages and the lessons are short enough that they can be done anywhere. You can choose to speak and have your diction analyzed, or while waiting for an appt, listen to a lesson. Easiest app to use and excellent teaching techniques so can you not only learn to speak, but also write in your chosen language.","2020-12",3,"+short"],[5,"Linguist here. I love Babbel! I used it to learn Turkish while living in Istanbul, and it was an excellent tool to advance not only my vocabulary & grammar, but also my understanding of social context factors. Lessons progress in an engaging and functional way: mnemonic pictures, dialogue fill-ins—no isolated nonsense sentences that you would never actually say. Babbel is integrative, useful, and even fun. Nowadays I use it to keep up on my Spanish since I'm back in the States. Thank you!","2020-05",3,"+fun"],[1,"I am trying to learn Russian, and I can say while I am learning, this app pushes you off the deep end WAY too fast. You are supposed to just understand things immediately as if it was natural, well, writing a foreign language language isn't natural. I dread every __________, and having vocabulary pictures presented for words I haven't learned yet in one frame, and having to phonically spell them one frame later. This wouldn't be bad, but these are high end words I will likely never use.","2020-05",2,""],[1,"The app barely gives you any trial for free to test it out and see if you'd like a subscription. It pushes hard to get you to sign up. I'm very angry because I signed up because it offers specifically Castilian Spanish, but the Castilian Spanish course teaches Latin American Spanish anyway!! What a rip-off. I just want to learn the Spanish spoken in Spain, but the app falsely advertised the course. Babbel's response implies I picked the wrong course, which I did not. So hard, it's discouraging.","2023-07",2,"pay,ad"],[1,"I work all day and I only have time in the evening, and there are no Italian classes after 5 on most days. I have had the same problem in French and from what I've seen, German. The customer service is unhelpful and says that they will add a request. I have sent so many emails. There is also not many languages. Other people in the western hemisphere have been complaining. I have bought a 6-month subscription. Why would you advertise so much in the US if you can't service our needs correctly?","2023-01",2,"pay,ad,cs"],[1,"Using Babbel to try to learn Spanish and failing miserably. More frustrating than helpful. No tips, direction or instruction before lessons, only after you've tried to guess your way through. No explanations as to why language usages are how they are, they just are. Method of instruction seems to be to throw you into the fray and let you flail about, then tell you what you did wrong after the fact. Bought 1 year subscription and regret it. Having much more luck with Duolingo - and it's free.","2020-04",2,"pay"],[2,"Not a fan of the way they teach you a language. I don't understand why they choose to teach us the things they do, it just doesn't make sense. Moves too fast and expects you to have something completely memorized after only seeing it once or twice. I dreaded doing it every day and the lessons took a little too long sometimes, but I bought 3 months of it so I kept going. I got to a point where I had absolutely no idea what the words in from of me said and I couldn't even guess, so I just gave up.","2020-10",2,""],[3,"i like it more than Duolingo so far, i remember my lessons better and they feel more practical. that being said, i'm doing the Swedish course, and i swear i could literally record the speaker and play it back and the app would still say the pronunciation is wrong. i don't know what it wants from me, i asked a Swedish friend to grade my pronunciations and he said they were excellent, yet the app outright refuses to recognize even the most simple words like \"vi\" and \"gata\".","2026-08",2,"voice,+effect,+short,+listen"],[3,"this app is just okay. for some reason the way they have the microphone set up during speaking lessons always cuts off the first half-second of your response, so it will mark it wrong nine times out of 10 unless you make some noise before you respond. Also, when accessing about 1/3 of the app I'm always greeted with a message saying that 'something went wrong'. it might help with troubleshooting if the message was more detailed than that. I also do not find navigating the menu very intuitive.","2026-08",2,"voice"],[3,"I have only been using this app for a couple of days so my opinion will probably change but... nothing in my responses while signing up for this app could possibly be interpreted to indicate that I was in any way interested in learning about someone's marital or dating status. nevertheless, that's what I had to endure for my first few lessons. I hope the lessons in the future more closely match my needs.","2026-07",2,"data,wish,+wish"],[4,"The service is amazing, the way they teach you phrases is intuitive and a lot of the phrases actually apply to real life. The only reason why this is a 4 star review is because on a Moto E it appears you cannot use the phone's default keyboard and you have to use the keyboard that is in the app. For me this causes issues with spelling things right because the scaling of the keys are different.","2021-05",2,"+review"],[4,"I've just completed 12 courses in a week, and I can confidently say I can read and write most of the common words and phrases so far of the language I'm learning. This app makes it really easy and fast to learn. I just wish I could review the words and phrases in a study form like the flash cards or filling in a sentence. That'd make it so much greater and easier then trying to go through the different courses again. Other than that, I love it and thank you so much for making it easy to learn!","2021-03",2,"+short,+review,+wish"],[5,"I have never attempted to learn an additional language in my life and have been pleasantly surprised by how easy they make the lessons to be understood reviewed and remembered with their process of turning things from your short-term memory into long-term memory makes the lessons I'm taking actually stick. I didn't expect learning another language to be so easy but they make it so","2022-08",2,"+effect,+short,+review"],[5,"I've enjoyed using this app to review and relearn Spanish. My only criticism is that I wish there was more vocal exercises rather than saying one word or a specific phrase. If there was a segment in here that allowed reading sentences out loud whilst being recorded, that would, I feel, be more affective for the learning process. And yes, I understand you can do that whilst practising without needing a recorded sentence segment, but it would be nice to be critiqued how you speak.","2020-05",2,"+review,+fun,+wish"],[5,"I have used other language learning apps such as Duolingo, memrise ect... They are all decent ways to learn a language for free but I must say paying for a year of Spanish from babbel is well worth it! I'm learning Spanish and I love how they give you conversations to use the words you have learned. Its a great app I highly recommend, also if you are the fence about paying it gives you a lesson for free so you can determine if it is worth it. Good luck!","2020-01",2,"+effect,+free"],[1,"I'd really like to rate but i can't log in after i paid. App didn't recognize my email, sent password resets, didn't get any emails, only to find out, i didn't spell my email correctly 😡 Strange thing, I was logged in, on the website, on my mobile, and unable to change email! Now i can't sign in at all. Going to write to support, bracing myself for long wait time since everyone is complaining about it. Update 13 feb 23: forgot to mention i paid for this service!","2023-02",1,"data"],[1,"I thought this app would be the perfect language app for me, but I could only do one lesson because I was using a free account and I would really like it if there could be more lessons open to the people that don't want to pay for their account, because I was disappointed by that. The reason I did not pay is the fact that they demand so much money, and I feel like they should drop the price, otherwise, it is a money waster, you are better off with Duolingo.","2020-04",1,"pay,data"],[2,"This is the 5th method I have used to study German, and my least favorite. It forces you to be able to write, which is very hard when you are first starting and all you want is to be able to speak and understand a language. Update: I agree writing can be important, but it depends on your reason for learning. I'm just traveling, so i want the basics. Your ads claim to learn it fast, so I assume that would be the target use.","2019-08",1,"ad"],[3,"I find the idiomatic translations confusing and unhelpful for learning non-idiomatic words and phrases. The absent relevant lessons before testing is always annoying. The app automatically moves on immediately after a question, which doesn't allow for learning, so I have to manually go backwards in the quiz to stare at the sentence to try to understand and memorize the words or concepts. Liking Babbel less and less with time. Doubt I'll renew the subscription.","2026-08",1,"pay,ui,+effect,+exam"],[4,"I did enjoy using Babbel but I can't get past course 3 and lesson 4 review, the app is freezing and not loading to the next slide/question/flash card. I click on lesson 5 and there is also no audio coming out at all either when I press the speaker icon to hear audio.. I did pay for full price for the 12 month subscription a few days ago.. I hope that these issues can be resolved because if not then I'm going to look into getting my money back..","2022-05",1,"+review,+fun,+listen,+wish"],[5,"He estado usando este programa desde 2018 de julio, pero toma tan largo a abrir... I'll still give it 5 stars because I can read / speak / write in spanish because of (not perfect mind you, I still make mistakes) Babbel, I basically wrote in spanish that this app takes too long to load up I have to close the app than reopen. But you'll definitely learn your target language.. Just stick it out guys don't give up.. I've been at it since the summer of 2018. The loading needs fixing, that's all.","2020-03",1,""],[5,"I took a free lesson and bought a 6mo course after. Anyone who is serious in acquiring a second language should use this app; it is a solid base.The read, write, speak technique with spaced repitition is KEY! IMO, taking each lesson more than once helps to absorb the material. There are practical conversations in the target language, and the lessons can be done in 15 min. Babbel is one of the most used app on my phone. Once i complete the Spanish course I will repurchase and do it all over. 5/5","2020-04",1,"+effect,+review,+free"],[5,"Hi, I like the app and I improved my German a lot. I have few suggestions:1) I would like to remove the fixed lenght for exercise since I always correct myself looking at the lenght that is not for the best. 2) i would like to add grammar to my vocabulary and do the review as usual 3) i would like to perform only the review of the lessons to recall the old topics. Now i can do that but i cannot track how many times i reviewed the old lessons.","2020-04",1,"+effect,+review,+wish"],[5,"Price is a factor, but as somebody who has used it to get by in Germany after moving here with my spouse, so far so good. I wish it had started sooner with this app for my learning style. I do wish there was a better understanding of topics covered in terms of language certification, because I'm part way through A2 and I'm only now covering A1 test material it seems. Conversationally it's been extremely helpful though to navigate day-to-day activity.","2022-11",1,"+effect,+exam,+wish"],[5,"Okay this is so cool. I have started learning German words and phrases in less than an hour. This is not a joke y'all. My sister came how and I was like HALLO ICH BIN RANDY This is definitely worth a try and I would 100 percent recommend this app to anyone who wants to learn a new language or improve their current ones! First lesson was great and I will be subscribing to their super affordable payment options!!!!!!","2020-04",1,"+wish"],[5,"Fantastic! I LOVE Babbel. It makes language-learning fun and easy. It's been a great way to catch back up on my French. I especially like how you can review your lessons in different formats (speaking, writing, flashcards, listening.) I think it's good to mix up your review approach to exercise different muscles in your brain.","2020-03",1,"+short,+review,+fun,+listen"],[5,"So user friendly! I love the way lessons are structured, the variety of learning styles incorporated, and the conversational nature of lessons instead of just vocab and grammar. I took 6 years of French in my youth and have been much more able to string sentences together with this app than all the lessons I've had before.","2020-06",1,""],[2,"It was amazing at first; had a nice layout, worked on speech and listening ext. Then it went downhill. As soon as I finished my first lesson it told me to subscribe to keep doing lessons. I think it would be really good if you had the money to pay, but I wouldn't bother if you don't. Overall, its a good app I'd just like to see more lessons being free, or maybe free with ads.","2026-07",0,"pay,ad,voice,ui"]];